window.I4_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Ocean Zones & Geography 海洋分區與地理","cards":[{"w":"seabed","p":"n.","d":"the ground at the bottom of the sea","c":"海床","s":"The divers found an old anchor lying on the sandy seabed, and they carefully brought it up to the boat.","t":"潛水員在沙質的海床上發現一個老舊的錨,他們小心地把它帶上船。"},{"w":"trench","p":"n.","d":"a very deep, narrow valley in the ocean floor","c":"海溝","s":"The Mariana trench is deeper than Mount Everest is tall, so very few people have ever reached its bottom.","t":"馬里亞納海溝比聖母峰還要深,所以極少有人曾到達它的底部。"},{"w":"abyss","p":"n.","d":"a very deep place that seems to have no bottom","c":"深淵","s":"The documentary showed strange fish living in the dark abyss, where sunlight never reaches and the water is freezing cold.","t":"這部紀錄片介紹了住在黑暗深淵裡的奇特魚類,那裡陽光永遠照不到,而且海水冰冷刺骨。"},{"w":"abyssal","p":"adj.","d":"found in the deepest parts of the ocean","c":"深海底層的","s":"Scientists know very little about abyssal animals because they live thousands of metres down, and their habitat is hard to reach.","t":"科學家對深海底層的動物所知甚少,因為牠們住在數千公尺深的地方,而且牠們的棲地很難抵達。"},{"w":"continental shelf","p":"n.phr.","d":"the shallow sea floor near the edge of a continent","c":"大陸棚","s":"Most fish are caught on the continental shelf because the water there is shallow, and sunlight helps plants and plankton grow.","t":"大部分的魚是在大陸棚捕獲的,因為那裡的海水較淺,而且陽光能幫助植物和浮游生物生長。"},{"w":"ridge","p":"n.","d":"a long, narrow line of high land or mountains","c":"海脊;山脊","s":"A huge underwater ridge runs through the middle of the Atlantic, and new sea floor slowly forms along it.","t":"一條巨大的海底海脊貫穿大西洋中部,新的海床沿著它慢慢形成。"},{"w":"basin","p":"n.","d":"a large, low area of land or sea floor shaped like a bowl","c":"盆地;海盆","s":"The Pacific Ocean basin is the largest on Earth, and it covers almost one third of the planet's surface.","t":"太平洋海盆是地球上最大的,它幾乎覆蓋了地球表面的三分之一。"},{"w":"seamount","p":"n.","d":"an underwater mountain that does not reach the surface","c":"海底山","s":"Sharks often gather around a seamount because food is plentiful there, so fishermen like to visit these underwater mountains.","t":"鯊魚常常聚集在海底山附近,因為那裡食物豐富,所以漁民喜歡造訪這些海底山。"},{"w":"strait","p":"n.","d":"a narrow area of sea that joins two larger seas","c":"海峽","s":"Ferries cross the Taiwan strait every day, but the trip can be rough when strong winds blow in winter.","t":"渡輪每天橫越台灣海峽,但冬天颳強風時航程可能會很顛簸。"},{"w":"gulf","p":"n.","d":"a large area of sea mostly surrounded by land","c":"海灣(大型)","s":"Many oil platforms stand in the gulf of Mexico, and they have caused serious pollution after accidents in the past.","t":"墨西哥灣有許多石油平台,而且它們過去在意外發生後造成了嚴重的污染。"},{"w":"bay","p":"n.","d":"a part of the sea that curves into the land","c":"海灣","s":"We rented kayaks and paddled around the quiet bay, while our parents relaxed on the beach and read their books.","t":"我們租了獨木舟在寧靜的海灣划船,而我們的父母則在海灘上放鬆看書。"},{"w":"lagoon","p":"n.","d":"an area of calm sea water separated from the ocean by sand or reef","c":"潟湖","s":"The water in the lagoon is calm and warm, so it is a safe place for children to swim and snorkel.","t":"潟湖裡的海水平靜又溫暖,所以對孩子來說是游泳和浮潛的安全地方。"},{"w":"inlet","p":"n.","d":"a narrow area of water that goes into the land from the sea","c":"小海灣;水灣","s":"Small fishing boats hide in the inlet during typhoons, because the hills around it block the strongest winds.","t":"颱風期間小漁船會躲在小海灣裡,因為周圍的山丘能擋住最強的風。"},{"w":"peninsula","p":"n.","d":"land almost surrounded by water but joined to a larger area","c":"半島","s":"Hengchun is on a peninsula in southern Taiwan, so visitors can see the sea on three sides of the town.","t":"恆春位在台灣南部的一個半島上,所以遊客可以在小鎮的三面看見大海。"},{"w":"archipelago","p":"n.","d":"a group of many islands","c":"群島","s":"The Philippines is a large archipelago of over 7,000 islands, and many people travel between them by boat.","t":"菲律賓是一個由超過七千座島嶼組成的大群島,許多人搭船往返於島嶼之間。"},{"w":"atoll","p":"n.","d":"a ring-shaped coral island around a lagoon","c":"環礁","s":"The tiny atoll is only two metres above the sea, so rising water is a serious danger for the people living there.","t":"這個小環礁只高出海面兩公尺,所以上升的海水對住在那裡的人是嚴重的危險。"},{"w":"shoreline","p":"n.","d":"the edge of the sea where it meets the land","c":"海岸線","s":"Volunteers walked along the shoreline for three hours, and they collected more than fifty bags of rubbish.","t":"志工們沿著海岸線走了三個小時,他們收集了超過五十袋垃圾。"},{"w":"shallows","p":"n.","d":"an area of shallow water","c":"淺灘;淺水區","s":"Young fish stay in the shallows near the beach because big predators cannot easily follow them there.","t":"幼魚待在海灘附近的淺水區,因為大型掠食者不容易跟著牠們到那裡。"},{"w":"depth","p":"n.","d":"how deep something is","c":"深度","s":"The submarine reached a depth of 3,000 metres, but the crew had to return because the battery was getting low.","t":"潛水艇到達了三千公尺的深度,但組員必須返航,因為電池電量越來越低。"},{"w":"surface","p":"n.","d":"the top layer of water or land","c":"表面;水面","s":"The whale came up to the surface to breathe, and everyone on the boat cheered when they saw its huge tail.","t":"那頭鯨魚浮上水面呼吸,船上的每個人看到牠巨大的尾巴時都歡呼了起來。"},{"w":"sunlit","p":"adj.","d":"receiving light from the sun","c":"陽光照射的","s":"Most ocean life lives in the sunlit top layer of the sea, because plants there can use light to make food.","t":"大部分的海洋生物生活在海洋陽光照射的最上層,因為那裡的植物能利用光來製造食物。"},{"w":"twilight zone","p":"n.phr.","d":"the dim ocean layer between about 200 and 1,000 metres deep","c":"中層帶;暮光帶","s":"Very little light reaches the twilight zone, so many fish there have huge eyes to help them see.","t":"極少光線能到達暮光帶,所以那裡的許多魚有巨大的眼睛幫助牠們看見東西。"},{"w":"hydrothermal vent","p":"n.phr.","d":"a crack in the sea floor that lets out very hot water","c":"熱泉噴口","s":"Scientists were surprised to find crabs and worms living near a hydrothermal vent, although the water there was extremely hot.","t":"科學家驚訝地發現螃蟹和蠕蟲生活在熱泉噴口附近,儘管那裡的水極度炙熱。"},{"w":"upwelling","p":"n.","d":"the rising of cold, deep water to the surface","c":"湧升流","s":"upwelling brings cold, nutrient-rich water to the surface, so the area becomes an excellent place for fishing.","t":"湧升流把寒冷、富含養分的海水帶到表面,所以這個區域成為絕佳的漁場。"},{"w":"gyre","p":"n.","d":"a large system of circular ocean currents","c":"環流","s":"Floating rubbish gets trapped in the North Pacific gyre, and it slowly forms a huge area of plastic waste.","t":"漂浮的垃圾被困在北太平洋環流中,而且慢慢形成一大片塑膠垃圾區。"},{"w":"swell","p":"n.","d":"long, smooth waves caused by distant winds","c":"湧浪","s":"Surfers were excited about the big swell that arrived after the storm, but the lifeguards warned beginners to stay out.","t":"衝浪者對暴風雨過後來的大湧浪感到興奮,但救生員警告初學者不要下水。"},{"w":"undertow","p":"n.","d":"a strong current under the surface that pulls water away from the shore","c":"退浪;底流","s":"The beach looked calm, but a dangerous undertow pulled the swimmer away from the shore, so a lifeguard had to rescue him.","t":"海灘看起來很平靜,但危險的底流把泳客拉離岸邊,所以救生員必須救他。"},{"w":"tsunami","p":"n.","d":"a very large wave caused by an earthquake under the sea","c":"海嘯","s":"After the earthquake, a tsunami warning was sent to everyone's phones, and families quickly moved to higher ground.","t":"地震之後,海嘯警報發送到每個人的手機,家家戶戶迅速移往高處。"},{"w":"offshore","p":"adj.","d":"located in the sea, away from the coast","c":"離岸的;近海的","s":"The government plans to build more offshore wind farms, because the wind at sea is stronger and more reliable.","t":"政府計畫興建更多離岸風場,因為海上的風更強、更穩定。"},{"w":"inshore","p":"adj.","d":"in the sea but close to the land","c":"近岸的","s":"inshore fishing boats are small, so they usually stay close to the coast and return to the harbour every evening.","t":"近岸漁船很小,所以通常待在海岸附近,而且每天傍晚返回港口。"},{"w":"maritime","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the sea or ships","c":"海事的;航海的","s":"Taiwan has a long maritime history, and the museum in Keelung shows how people traded by sea centuries ago.","t":"台灣有悠久的海洋歷史,而基隆的博物館展示了幾百年前人們如何透過海路貿易。"},{"w":"oceanic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the ocean","c":"海洋的","s":"oceanic islands like Hawaii were formed by volcanoes, so their plants and animals arrived from far away.","t":"像夏威夷這樣的海洋島嶼是由火山形成的,所以島上的動植物是從遠方來的。"},{"w":"cove","p":"n.","d":"a small, sheltered bay","c":"小海灣","s":"We found a hidden cove with clear blue water, and we spent the whole afternoon swimming there without other tourists.","t":"我們發現了一個海水清澈湛藍的隱密小海灣,整個下午都在那裡游泳,沒有其他遊客。"},{"w":"high seas","p":"n.phr.","d":"the open ocean that no country controls","c":"公海","s":"Fishing on the high seas is hard to control because no single country owns those waters.","t":"在公海捕魚很難管控,因為沒有任何單一國家擁有那片水域。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Marine Life 海洋生物","cards":[{"w":"plankton","p":"n.","d":"tiny plants and animals that float in the sea","c":"浮游生物","s":"Many large whales eat plankton, although these tiny living things are almost too small to see.","t":"許多大型鯨魚以浮游生物為食,儘管這些微小的生物小到幾乎看不見。"},{"w":"phytoplankton","p":"n.","d":"tiny plants that float in the sea and use sunlight","c":"浮游植物","s":"phytoplankton produces a large part of the oxygen we breathe, so the health of the ocean matters to everyone.","t":"浮游植物製造了我們呼吸的大部分氧氣,所以海洋的健康對每個人都很重要。"},{"w":"zooplankton","p":"n.","d":"tiny animals that float in the sea","c":"浮游動物","s":"Small fish feed on zooplankton at night, and then bigger fish come to hunt those small fish.","t":"小魚在夜間以浮游動物為食,然後更大的魚會來獵捕那些小魚。"},{"w":"krill","p":"n.","d":"small shrimp-like animals eaten by whales and penguins","c":"磷蝦","s":"Blue whales can eat four tonnes of krill a day, so they need huge areas of rich, cold water.","t":"藍鯨一天可以吃掉四噸的磷蝦,所以牠們需要廣大、豐富又寒冷的水域。"},{"w":"jellyfish","p":"n.","d":"a soft sea animal with long parts that can sting","c":"水母","s":"My sister was stung by a jellyfish while she was swimming, so we put vinegar on her arm right away.","t":"我妹妹游泳時被水母螫到,所以我們立刻在她手臂上塗醋。"},{"w":"octopus","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with a soft body and eight arms","c":"章魚","s":"The octopus can change its colour in seconds, and it often hides between rocks to avoid hungry predators.","t":"章魚能在幾秒內改變顏色,而且牠常常躲在岩石之間躲避飢餓的掠食者。"},{"w":"squid","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with ten arms and a long body","c":"魷魚","s":"Fishermen use bright lights at night to attract squid, and the boats look like floating stars from the shore.","t":"漁民在夜間使用明亮的燈光吸引魷魚,從岸邊看,那些船就像漂浮的星星。"},{"w":"crustacean","p":"n.","d":"an animal with a hard shell, such as a crab or shrimp","c":"甲殼類動物","s":"A crab is a crustacean, so it has a hard shell, and it must grow a new one as its body gets bigger.","t":"螃蟹是甲殼類動物,所以牠有堅硬的殼,而且當身體長大時必須長出新殼。"},{"w":"crab","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with a shell, eight legs and two claws","c":"螃蟹","s":"The little crab walked sideways across the sand, and it quickly disappeared into a hole when we came closer.","t":"那隻小螃蟹橫著走過沙灘,我們靠近時牠迅速消失在一個洞裡。"},{"w":"lobster","p":"n.","d":"a large shellfish with big claws that people eat","c":"龍蝦","s":"lobster is an expensive dish in many restaurants, but some people refuse to eat it because they worry about overfishing.","t":"龍蝦在許多餐廳是昂貴的菜餚,但有些人拒絕吃,因為他們擔心過度捕撈。"},{"w":"shellfish","p":"n.","d":"sea animals with shells that people eat, like clams and shrimp","c":"貝類;有殼海鮮","s":"My uncle cannot eat shellfish because it makes his skin itchy, so he always orders fish instead.","t":"我叔叔不能吃有殼海鮮,因為那會讓他皮膚發癢,所以他總是改點魚。"},{"w":"mollusc","p":"n.","d":"a soft animal often with a shell, like a snail or octopus","c":"軟體動物","s":"An octopus is a mollusc without a shell, while a snail is one that carries its shell on its back.","t":"章魚是沒有殼的軟體動物,而蝸牛則是背著殼的軟體動物。"},{"w":"clam","p":"n.","d":"a shellfish with two shells that close tightly","c":"蛤蜊","s":"We dug clam out of the wet sand at low tide, and my grandmother cooked them in a delicious soup.","t":"我們在退潮時從濕沙裡挖出蛤蜊,而奶奶把牠們煮成美味的湯。"},{"w":"oyster","p":"n.","d":"a shellfish that can make pearls and is often eaten raw","c":"牡蠣;蚵仔","s":"Changhua is famous for its oyster farms, and visitors love to try the local oyster omelettes.","t":"彰化以牡蠣養殖場聞名,而遊客喜歡品嚐當地的蚵仔煎。"},{"w":"sea urchin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small round sea animal covered in sharp spines","c":"海膽","s":"Wear shoes when you walk on the rocks, because a sea urchin can hurt your feet badly with its sharp spines.","t":"在岩石上走路時要穿鞋,因為海膽會用牠尖銳的刺嚴重刺傷你的腳。"},{"w":"starfish","p":"n.","d":"a flat sea animal shaped like a star","c":"海星","s":"The children found a bright orange starfish in a rock pool, but their teacher asked them to put it back gently.","t":"孩子們在潮池裡發現一隻鮮橘色的海星,但老師請他們輕輕地把牠放回去。"},{"w":"sponge","p":"n.","d":"a simple sea animal with a body full of holes","c":"海綿","s":"A sponge looks like a plant, but it is actually an animal that filters food from the water.","t":"海綿看起來像植物,但牠其實是從水中過濾食物的動物。"},{"w":"seahorse","p":"n.","d":"a small fish with a head shaped like a horse","c":"海馬","s":"The male seahorse carries the babies in a pouch, and this makes it very unusual in the animal world.","t":"雄海馬把寶寶放在育兒袋中,這讓牠在動物界中非常特別。"},{"w":"shark","p":"n.","d":"a large fish with sharp teeth","c":"鯊魚","s":"Many people fear the shark, but it rarely attacks humans, and millions are killed every year for their fins.","t":"許多人害怕鯊魚,但牠很少攻擊人類,而且每年有數百萬隻因為魚鰭而被殺。"},{"w":"whale","p":"n.","d":"a very large sea mammal","c":"鯨魚","s":"We took a boat trip from Hualien to see a whale, and we were lucky enough to watch one jump out of the water.","t":"我們從花蓮搭船出海去看鯨魚,而且很幸運地看到一隻躍出水面。"},{"w":"dolphin","p":"n.","d":"an intelligent sea mammal with a long nose","c":"海豚","s":"A group of dolphin swam next to our boat, and they seemed to enjoy playing in the waves.","t":"一群海豚在我們的船旁邊游泳,牠們似乎很享受在浪中嬉戲。"},{"w":"seal","p":"n.","d":"a sea mammal with flippers that lives in cold places","c":"海豹","s":"A seal was lying on the rocks in the sun, and it did not seem worried by the tourists taking photos.","t":"一隻海豹躺在岩石上曬太陽,而且牠似乎一點也不在意拍照的遊客。"},{"w":"sea turtle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large turtle that lives in the ocean","c":"海龜","s":"A sea turtle swam slowly past us while we were snorkelling off Xiaoliuqiu, and we kept a respectful distance.","t":"我們在小琉球外海浮潛時,一隻海龜慢慢游過我們身邊,我們保持了尊重的距離。"},{"w":"seabird","p":"n.","d":"a bird that lives near the sea and eats fish","c":"海鳥","s":"The seabird dived into the water to catch a fish, but it accidentally swallowed a piece of plastic too.","t":"那隻海鳥衝進水裡抓魚,但牠也不小心吞下了一片塑膠。"},{"w":"penguin","p":"n.","d":"a black and white sea bird that cannot fly but swims well","c":"企鵝","s":"A penguin cannot fly, but it is an excellent swimmer, so it can catch fish easily under the ice.","t":"企鵝不會飛,但牠是很棒的游泳者,所以能輕鬆地在冰下捕魚。"},{"w":"gill","p":"n.","d":"the part of a fish used for breathing in water","c":"鰓","s":"Fish breathe through their gill, so they can take oxygen from the water but cannot live in the air.","t":"魚透過鰓呼吸,所以牠們能從水中取得氧氣,但無法在空氣中存活。"},{"w":"fin","p":"n.","d":"a thin flat part of a fish that helps it swim","c":"鰭","s":"We saw a dark fin above the water and thought it was a shark, but it turned out to be a friendly dolphin.","t":"我們看到水面上有一個深色的鰭,以為是鯊魚,但結果是一隻友善的海豚。"},{"w":"tentacle","p":"n.","d":"a long, thin arm of an animal like an octopus or jellyfish","c":"觸手","s":"The jellyfish's tentacle can be several metres long, so swimmers may be stung without even seeing it.","t":"水母的觸手可能長達好幾公尺,所以泳客甚至沒看到牠就可能被螫。"},{"w":"shell","p":"n.","d":"the hard outer cover of some animals","c":"殼;貝殼","s":"My little brother collected a beautiful shell from the beach, but I reminded him that some crabs need them as homes.","t":"我弟弟從海灘撿了一個美麗的貝殼,但我提醒他有些螃蟹需要它們當家。"},{"w":"blubber","p":"n.","d":"the thick layer of fat under the skin of whales and seals","c":"鯨脂;脂肪層","s":"Seals have a thick layer of blubber under their skin, so they can stay warm in icy water.","t":"海豹皮膚下有一層厚厚的脂肪層,所以牠們能在冰冷的水中保暖。"},{"w":"school","p":"n.","d":"a large group of fish swimming together","c":"魚群","s":"A huge school of silver fish moved together like one animal, and it quickly changed direction when a shark appeared.","t":"一大群銀色的魚群像一隻動物般一起移動,而且當鯊魚出現時迅速改變方向。"},{"w":"filter feeder","p":"n.phr.","d":"an animal that eats by straining tiny food from water","c":"濾食動物","s":"The whale shark is a filter feeder, so although it is huge, it only eats tiny plankton and small fish.","t":"鯨鯊是濾食動物,所以雖然牠很巨大,但只吃微小的浮游生物和小魚。"},{"w":"bioluminescent","p":"adj.","d":"able to produce its own light","c":"生物發光的","s":"The waves glowed blue at night because of bioluminescent plankton, and tourists came from far away to see it.","t":"因為會發光的浮游生物,海浪在夜裡發出藍光,遊客從遠方前來觀賞。"},{"w":"aquatic","p":"adj.","d":"living or growing in water","c":"水生的","s":"Frogs begin life as aquatic animals, but adult frogs can live on land as well as in water.","t":"青蛙一開始是水生動物,但成蛙既能在水中也能在陸地上生活。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Coral Reefs & Coastal Habitats 珊瑚礁與海岸棲地","cards":[{"w":"polyp","p":"n.","d":"a tiny soft animal that builds coral","c":"珊瑚蟲;水螅體","s":"Each coral polyp is smaller than a grain of rice, but millions of them together can build a huge reef.","t":"每一隻珊瑚蟲都比一粒米還小,但數百萬隻聚在一起就能建造巨大的珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"symbiosis","p":"n.","d":"a close relationship between two living things that helps both","c":"共生","s":"Coral and tiny algae live in symbiosis, because the algae make food for the coral while the coral gives them a safe home.","t":"珊瑚和微小的藻類處於共生關係,因為藻類為珊瑚製造食物,而珊瑚給它們一個安全的家。"},{"w":"symbiotic","p":"adj.","d":"helping each other by living closely together","c":"共生的","s":"The clownfish and the anemone have a symbiotic relationship, so the fish gets protection while the anemone gets cleaned.","t":"小丑魚和海葵有共生關係,所以魚得到保護,而海葵得到清潔。"},{"w":"kelp","p":"n.","d":"a very large, brown seaweed","c":"海帶;巨藻","s":"Sea otters live among tall kelp in California, and they often wrap themselves in it so they do not float away while sleeping.","t":"海獺生活在加州高大的巨藻間,而且牠們常把自己纏在裡面,這樣睡覺時才不會漂走。"},{"w":"seaweed","p":"n.","d":"a plant that grows in the sea","c":"海草;海藻","s":"Many Asian dishes use dried seaweed, and it is also becoming popular as a healthy snack in Western countries.","t":"許多亞洲料理使用乾海苔,而它在西方國家也逐漸成為受歡迎的健康零食。"},{"w":"seagrass","p":"n.","d":"grass-like plants that grow in shallow sea water","c":"海草床植物;海草","s":"Green turtles feed on seagrass in shallow bays, so protecting these underwater meadows also protects the turtles.","t":"綠蠵龜在淺海灣以海草為食,所以保護這些水下草原也就保護了海龜。"},{"w":"tide pool","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small pool of sea water left among rocks at low tide","c":"潮池","s":"The children spent the morning looking into a tide pool, and they found tiny fish, crabs and sea snails.","t":"孩子們整個早上都在觀察一個潮池,他們發現了小魚、螃蟹和海螺。"},{"w":"sandbar","p":"n.","d":"a long pile of sand in the sea near the coast","c":"沙洲","s":"Our boat got stuck on a sandbar at low tide, so we had to wait two hours for the water to rise again.","t":"我們的船在退潮時卡在沙洲上,所以我們必須等兩個小時讓海水再次上漲。"},{"w":"dune","p":"n.","d":"a hill of sand formed by the wind","c":"沙丘","s":"Grass helps hold each dune in place, so visitors are asked not to walk on the plants near the beach.","t":"草有助於讓每座沙丘保持在原位,所以遊客被要求不要踩踏海灘附近的植物。"},{"w":"intertidal","p":"adj.","d":"between the high and low tide lines","c":"潮間帶的","s":"Animals in the intertidal zone must survive both dry air and sea water, because the tide covers them only part of the day.","t":"潮間帶的動物必須在乾燥的空氣和海水中都能存活,因為潮水一天只淹沒牠們一段時間。"},{"w":"salt marsh","p":"n.phr.","d":"wet coastal land covered with grass and flooded by the tide","c":"鹽沼","s":"The salt marsh protects the village from storms, and it also provides food for thousands of birds every winter.","t":"鹽沼保護村莊免受暴風侵襲,而且每年冬天也為數千隻鳥提供食物。"},{"w":"cliff","p":"n.","d":"a high, steep rock face, often by the sea","c":"懸崖;峭壁","s":"Seabirds build their nests on the cliff above the sea, so foxes and other animals cannot reach their eggs.","t":"海鳥在海面上的懸崖築巢,所以狐狸和其他動物碰不到牠們的蛋。"},{"w":"shore","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of the sea","c":"岸邊;海岸","s":"We walked along the shore at sunset, and we watched the fishing boats coming back into the harbour.","t":"我們在日落時沿著海岸散步,看著漁船駛回港口。"},{"w":"pebble","p":"n.","d":"a small, smooth, round stone","c":"鵝卵石","s":"The beach at Qixingtan is covered with pebble instead of sand, so it makes a lovely sound when the waves pull back.","t":"七星潭的海灘上覆蓋著鵝卵石而不是沙子,所以當海浪退去時會發出美妙的聲音。"},{"w":"barnacle","p":"n.","d":"a small sea animal that sticks to rocks and ships","c":"藤壺","s":"Thousands of barnacle grew on the bottom of the boat, so it moved more slowly and used more fuel.","t":"數千隻藤壺長在船底,所以船移動得更慢,而且耗費更多燃料。"},{"w":"anemone","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with many soft arms that looks like a flower","c":"海葵","s":"The anemone looks like a colourful flower, but its soft arms can sting small fish that swim too close.","t":"海葵看起來像一朵色彩繽紛的花,但它柔軟的觸手會螫傷游得太近的小魚。"},{"w":"clownfish","p":"n.","d":"a small orange and white fish that lives in anemones","c":"小丑魚","s":"After the famous cartoon came out, many children wanted a clownfish as a pet, and wild numbers dropped in some places.","t":"那部知名卡通上映後,許多孩子想要養小丑魚當寵物,而某些地方的野生數量因此下降。"},{"w":"sea cucumber","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft sea animal shaped like a cucumber that lives on the sea floor","c":"海參","s":"A sea cucumber cleans the sea floor by eating sand and waste, but it is overharvested because some people consider it a luxury food.","t":"海參藉由吃沙子和廢物來清潔海床,但牠被過度採集,因為有些人把牠當作高級食材。"},{"w":"spawn","p":"v.","d":"to produce eggs in large numbers (of fish and other water animals)","c":"產卵","s":"Corals spawn on just a few nights each year, and divers travel far to see the water fill with tiny eggs.","t":"珊瑚每年只在少數幾個夜晚產卵,而潛水員遠道而來觀看海水充滿微小的卵。"},{"w":"larva","p":"n.","d":"a very young form of an animal before it changes into an adult","c":"幼體;幼蟲","s":"Each coral larva drifts in the ocean for days, and then it settles on a rock to start a new colony.","t":"每一隻珊瑚幼體在海洋中漂流好幾天,然後它會附著在岩石上開始一個新的群體。"},{"w":"nursery","p":"n.","d":"a place where young animals grow up safely","c":"育幼場","s":"Mangrove roots are a nursery for young fish, because larger fish cannot swim between the thick roots.","t":"紅樹林的根部是幼魚的育幼場,因為較大的魚無法在茂密的根之間游動。"},{"w":"limestone","p":"n.","d":"a type of white or grey rock formed from shells and coral","c":"石灰岩","s":"Kenting's coastline is made of limestone that was once an ancient coral reef, and you can still see fossils in the rocks.","t":"墾丁的海岸線是由曾經是古老珊瑚礁的石灰岩構成的,而你仍能在岩石中看到化石。"},{"w":"skeleton","p":"n.","d":"the hard structure that supports a body","c":"骨骼","s":"When coral dies, its white skeleton remains on the reef, but seaweed soon grows over it.","t":"珊瑚死亡時,它白色的骨骼會留在礁上,但海藻很快就會長滿在上面。"},{"w":"calcium","p":"n.","d":"a chemical element found in bones, shells and coral","c":"鈣","s":"Coral uses calcium from sea water to build its hard skeleton, but warmer, more acidic water makes this harder.","t":"珊瑚利用海水中的鈣建造堅硬的骨骼,但更溫暖、更酸的海水讓這件事變得更困難。"},{"w":"snorkel","p":"v.","d":"to swim near the surface with a tube to breathe through","c":"浮潛","s":"We went to snorkel near Green Island, and we saw colourful fish only a few metres from the beach.","t":"我們到綠島附近浮潛,而且在離海灘只有幾公尺的地方就看到色彩繽紛的魚。"},{"w":"scuba diving","p":"n.phr.","d":"swimming deep underwater with an air tank","c":"水肺潛水","s":"My cousin took a scuba diving course last summer, and now she can explore reefs twenty metres underwater.","t":"我表姊去年夏天上了水肺潛水課程,現在她可以探索水下二十公尺的珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"no-take zone","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sea area where all fishing and collecting are banned","c":"禁漁區","s":"Fishing is completely banned in the no-take zone, so fish numbers there have grown quickly over the past ten years.","t":"在禁漁區內完全禁止捕魚,所以那裡的魚群數量在過去十年快速成長。"},{"w":"lifeguard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to watch and rescue swimmers","c":"救生員","s":"The lifeguard blew his whistle loudly, because a group of teenagers were swimming outside the safe area.","t":"救生員大聲吹哨,因為一群青少年在安全區域外游泳。"},{"w":"rip current","p":"n.phr.","d":"a strong current that flows quickly away from the beach","c":"離岸流","s":"If a rip current pulls you out to sea, swim parallel to the beach instead of fighting against the water.","t":"如果離岸流把你拉向外海,要與海灘平行地游,而不是逆著水流掙扎。"},{"w":"breakwater","p":"n.","d":"a wall built into the sea to protect a harbour from waves","c":"防波堤","s":"The new breakwater protects the harbour from big waves, but some people worry that it has changed the beach nearby.","t":"新的防波堤保護港口不受大浪侵襲,但有些人擔心它改變了附近的海灘。"},{"w":"pier","p":"n.","d":"a long structure built from the land out over the sea","c":"碼頭;突堤","s":"We walked to the end of the pier to watch the sunset, and an old man there was fishing quietly.","t":"我們走到碼頭盡頭看夕陽,那裡有一位老人正安靜地釣魚。"},{"w":"lighthouse","p":"n.","d":"a tower with a bright light that warns ships of danger","c":"燈塔","s":"The old lighthouse at Eluanbi has guided ships for over a hundred years, and it is now a popular tourist spot.","t":"鵝鑾鼻的老燈塔已經為船隻導航超過一百年,而它現在是熱門的觀光景點。"},{"w":"shoal","p":"n.","d":"a large group of fish swimming together","c":"魚群","s":"A shoal of sardines turned silver in the sunlight, and the divers watched as it twisted and turned around them.","t":"一群沙丁魚魚群在陽光下閃著銀光,潛水員看著牠們在身邊扭轉迴旋。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Ocean Science & Exploration 海洋科學與探索","cards":[{"w":"oceanography","p":"n.","d":"the scientific study of the ocean","c":"海洋學","s":"My cousin is studying oceanography at university, and she spends a month at sea every year collecting water samples.","t":"我表姊在大學讀海洋學,而且她每年都會在海上待一個月採集海水樣本。"},{"w":"oceanographer","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies the ocean","c":"海洋學家","s":"An oceanographer explained on TV that the ocean is getting warmer, and she warned that fish are moving to cooler waters.","t":"一位海洋學家在電視上解釋海洋正在變暖,而且她警告魚類正遷往較涼的水域。"},{"w":"marine biologist","p":"n.phr.","d":"a scientist who studies living things in the sea","c":"海洋生物學家","s":"I want to become a marine biologist because I love sea animals, and I hope to help protect coral reefs one day.","t":"我想成為海洋生物學家,因為我熱愛海洋動物,而且我希望有一天能幫忙保護珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"submarine","p":"n.","d":"a ship that can travel underwater","c":"潛水艇","s":"The tourist submarine took us forty metres under the sea, and we watched sharks through the large windows.","t":"觀光潛水艇帶我們到海面下四十公尺,我們透過大窗戶觀看鯊魚。"},{"w":"submersible","p":"n.","d":"a small underwater vehicle used for research","c":"深潛器","s":"The scientists used a submersible to reach the deep sea floor, because divers cannot survive the pressure there.","t":"科學家使用深潛器抵達深海海床,因為潛水員無法承受那裡的壓力。"},{"w":"sonar","p":"n.","d":"a system that uses sound to find objects underwater","c":"聲納","s":"The ship used sonar to map the sea floor, but scientists worry that the loud sounds may confuse whales.","t":"這艘船使用聲納繪製海床地圖,但科學家擔心巨大的聲響可能讓鯨魚感到混亂。"},{"w":"buoy","p":"n.","d":"a floating object in the sea used as a marker or to measure things","c":"浮標","s":"A yellow buoy floats above the reef to show boats where they can tie up, so they do not drop anchors on the coral.","t":"一個黃色浮標漂浮在珊瑚礁上方,告訴船隻可以在哪裡繫泊,這樣它們就不會把錨丟在珊瑚上。"},{"w":"probe","p":"n.","d":"a tool sent to collect information from a place that is hard to reach","c":"探測器","s":"Researchers lowered a probe into the deep water, and it sent back data about temperature and oxygen levels.","t":"研究人員把探測器放入深水中,它傳回有關溫度和氧氣含量的數據。"},{"w":"expedition","p":"n.","d":"an organised journey to explore or study something","c":"探險;考察","s":"The team went on a three-month expedition to Antarctica, and they discovered several new kinds of sea creatures.","t":"團隊前往南極進行為期三個月的考察,而且他們發現了好幾種新的海洋生物。"},{"w":"explorer","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to unknown places to learn about them","c":"探險家","s":"The famous ocean explorer spent his life studying the sea, and his films made millions of people love marine life.","t":"這位著名的海洋探險家一生都在研究海洋,而他的影片讓數百萬人愛上海洋生物。"},{"w":"navigate","p":"v.","d":"to find the way when travelling, especially by sea","c":"導航;航行","s":"Ancient sailors used the stars to navigate across the Pacific, although they had no maps or modern instruments.","t":"古代水手利用星星航行橫越太平洋,儘管他們沒有地圖或現代儀器。"},{"w":"navigation","p":"n.","d":"the skill of planning and following a route","c":"導航;航海術","s":"Modern navigation depends on satellites, but sailors still learn to use maps in case the electronic system fails.","t":"現代導航仰賴衛星,但水手仍然學習使用地圖,以防電子系統故障。"},{"w":"voyage","p":"n.","d":"a long journey by sea","c":"航程;航行","s":"The voyage from Taiwan to Japan took three days, and many passengers felt seasick during the stormy weather.","t":"從台灣到日本的航程花了三天,而且許多乘客在暴風雨天氣中感到暈船。"},{"w":"vessel","p":"n.","d":"a ship or large boat","c":"船隻;船艦","s":"The research vessel carries a small lab, so scientists can study samples while they are still at sea.","t":"這艘研究船上載有一間小實驗室,所以科學家仍在海上時就能研究樣本。"},{"w":"crew","p":"n.","d":"the people who work on a ship","c":"船員;全體工作人員","s":"The crew worked through the night to repair the engine, because the ship was drifting toward dangerous rocks.","t":"船員們徹夜工作修理引擎,因為船正漂向危險的岩石。"},{"w":"deep-sea","p":"adj.","d":"found or happening in the deepest parts of the ocean","c":"深海的","s":"deep-sea fish often look strange, and some have glowing lights that help them catch food in the dark.","t":"深海魚常常長得很奇特,而且有些有發光器幫助牠們在黑暗中捕捉食物。"},{"w":"water pressure","p":"n.phr.","d":"the force of water pushing on something","c":"水壓","s":"water pressure increases as you go deeper, so divers must come up slowly to stay safe.","t":"水壓會隨著你潛得越深而增加,所以潛水員必須慢慢上升才能保持安全。"},{"w":"sediment","p":"n.","d":"sand, mud and stones that settle at the bottom of water","c":"沉積物","s":"Scientists study sediment from the sea floor, because it holds clues about the climate thousands of years ago.","t":"科學家研究海床的沉積物,因為它保存了數千年前氣候的線索。"},{"w":"chart","p":"v.","d":"to make a map of an area, especially of the sea","c":"繪製(海)圖","s":"Early sailors had to chart the coastline carefully, because hidden rocks could easily sink their ships.","t":"早期水手必須仔細繪製海岸線的地圖,因為隱藏的礁石很容易讓船沉沒。"},{"w":"dive","p":"v.","d":"to go under water, often with special equipment","c":"潛水","s":"We plan to dive near the shipwreck tomorrow, but the trip will be cancelled if the sea is too rough.","t":"我們計畫明天在沉船附近潛水,但如果海象太差,行程就會取消。"},{"w":"diver","p":"n.","d":"a person who swims underwater, often for work or sport","c":"潛水員","s":"The diver checked his air tank twice before jumping in, because a small mistake can be very dangerous underwater.","t":"那位潛水員跳下水前檢查了他的氣瓶兩次,因為在水下一個小錯誤就可能非常危險。"},{"w":"wetsuit","p":"n.","d":"a tight rubber suit that keeps you warm in water","c":"潛水衣;防寒衣","s":"The water was only eighteen degrees, so I wore a thick wetsuit and stayed warm for the whole dive.","t":"海水只有十八度,所以我穿了一件厚防寒衣,整趟潛水都保持溫暖。"},{"w":"underwater","p":"adj.","d":"below the surface of water","c":"水下的;水中的","s":"She bought an underwater camera before her holiday, and she took amazing photos of turtles and coral.","t":"她在假期前買了一台水下相機,而且拍了很棒的海龜和珊瑚照片。"},{"w":"satellite","p":"n.","d":"a machine in space that sends information back to Earth","c":"衛星","s":"Data from a satellite shows that sea temperatures are rising, so scientists can warn reef managers in advance.","t":"來自衛星的數據顯示海水溫度正在上升,所以科學家能事先警告珊瑚礁管理人員。"},{"w":"uncharted","p":"adj.","d":"not yet mapped or explored","c":"未知的;海圖上未標明的","s":"Large parts of the sea floor are still uncharted, so explorers may discover new mountains and canyons in the future.","t":"海床的大部分地區仍然未被繪製,所以探險家未來可能會發現新的山脈和峽谷。"},{"w":"unexplored","p":"adj.","d":"not yet visited or studied","c":"未探索的","s":"More than eighty percent of the ocean is unexplored, and scientists believe millions of species are still unknown.","t":"超過百分之八十的海洋尚未被探索,而且科學家相信仍有數百萬個物種不為人知。"},{"w":"compass","p":"n.","d":"a tool with a needle that always points north","c":"指南針;羅盤","s":"The sailor checked his compass because the clouds were hiding the stars, and he did not want to lose his way.","t":"那名水手查看他的指南針,因為雲層遮住了星星,而他不想迷失方向。"},{"w":"anchor","p":"n.","d":"a heavy metal object dropped to stop a boat from moving","c":"錨","s":"Boats should never drop an anchor on coral, because it can break plants and animals that took years to grow.","t":"船隻絕不應該把錨丟在珊瑚上,因為它會破壞花了好幾年才長成的動植物。"},{"w":"hull","p":"n.","d":"the main body of a ship","c":"船身;船體","s":"The hull of the ship was damaged by rocks, so water began to come in and the crew called for help.","t":"船的船體被岩石撞壞,所以海水開始流入,船員發出求救訊號。"},{"w":"harbour","p":"n.","d":"a sheltered area of water where ships can stay safely","c":"港口;港灣","s":"All the fishing boats returned to the harbour before the typhoon arrived, and the fishermen tied them together tightly.","t":"所有漁船在颱風來臨前回到港口,漁民們把船緊緊地綁在一起。"},{"w":"sink","p":"v.","d":"to go down below the surface of water","c":"下沉;沉沒","s":"The old ship hit an iceberg and sank in less than three hours, so many passengers did not have time to escape.","t":"那艘老船撞上冰山,不到三小時就沉沒了,所以許多乘客來不及逃生。"},{"w":"shipwreck","p":"n.","d":"the remains of a ship that has sunk","c":"沉船;船骸","s":"The shipwreck has become an artificial reef, and divers love to see the fish living inside it.","t":"這艘沉船已經成為人工魚礁,而潛水員喜歡觀看住在裡面的魚。"},{"w":"salvage","p":"v.","d":"to save goods or a ship from damage or the sea","c":"打撈;搶救","s":"The company tried to salvage the cargo from the sunken ship, but strong currents made the work very slow.","t":"公司試著從沉船中打撈貨物,但強勁的海流讓工作進行得非常緩慢。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Threats to the Ocean 海洋威脅","cards":[{"w":"microplastic","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of plastic less than 5 mm long","c":"塑膠微粒","s":"Scientists found microplastic in the stomachs of many fish, and some of these tiny pieces may end up in our food.","t":"科學家在許多魚的胃裡發現塑膠微粒,而這些微小碎片有些可能最後進入我們的食物。"},{"w":"oil spill","p":"n.phr.","d":"an accident in which oil escapes into the sea","c":"漏油;油污外洩","s":"The oil spill covered the beach in black oil, and volunteers spent weeks cleaning birds and rocks.","t":"漏油讓海灘覆蓋上黑色的油,志工們花了好幾週清洗鳥類和岩石。"},{"w":"runoff","p":"n.","d":"rain water that flows from land into rivers and the sea, carrying dirt and chemicals","c":"地表逕流","s":"Farm runoff carries fertiliser into the sea after heavy rain, so harmful algae can grow very quickly.","t":"大雨過後,農田逕流把肥料帶入海中,所以有害的藻類會迅速生長。"},{"w":"sewage","p":"n.","d":"dirty water and waste from toilets and drains","c":"污水","s":"Some coastal towns still release sewage straight into the sea, so swimmers may get sick after a day at the beach.","t":"一些沿海城鎮仍然把污水直接排入海中,所以泳客在海灘待一天後可能會生病。"},{"w":"dump","p":"v.","d":"to throw away waste in a careless or illegal way","c":"傾倒;丟棄","s":"Some factories secretly dump chemicals into rivers at night, but the waste still flows into the ocean.","t":"有些工廠在夜間偷偷把化學物質傾倒到河裡,但這些廢物仍會流入海洋。"},{"w":"beach clean-up","p":"n.phr.","d":"an event where people collect rubbish from a beach","c":"淨灘活動","s":"Our class joined a beach clean-up last Saturday, and we were shocked by how many bottle caps we found in the sand.","t":"我們班上週六參加了淨灘活動,而我們對在沙子裡找到那麼多瓶蓋感到震驚。"},{"w":"garbage patch","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large area of the ocean where floating rubbish collects","c":"垃圾帶","s":"The Great Pacific garbage patch is not a solid island, but it contains millions of small pieces of floating plastic.","t":"太平洋垃圾帶不是一座實心的島,但它含有數百萬片漂浮的小塑膠碎片。"},{"w":"ghost net","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fishing net that has been lost or left in the sea","c":"幽靈漁網","s":"A ghost net can keep catching fish for years after it is lost, so divers work hard to remove them from reefs.","t":"幽靈漁網遺失後仍能持續捕到魚好幾年,所以潛水員努力把它們從珊瑚礁上移除。"},{"w":"entangle","p":"v.","d":"to catch something so that it cannot get free","c":"纏住","s":"Old fishing lines can entangle turtles and seals, and many of these animals die because they cannot swim or eat.","t":"舊的釣魚線可能纏住海龜和海豹,而許多這些動物因為無法游泳或進食而死亡。"},{"w":"dead zone","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area of sea with too little oxygen for most life","c":"死區;缺氧區","s":"Fertiliser has created a dead zone near the river mouth, and almost no fish can survive there in summer.","t":"肥料在河口附近造成了一個死區,而夏天幾乎沒有魚能在那裡存活。"},{"w":"hypoxia","p":"n.","d":"a condition of having too little oxygen","c":"缺氧","s":"hypoxia in coastal waters is becoming more common, because warm water holds less oxygen than cold water.","t":"沿岸水域的缺氧現象越來越常見,因為溫水所含的氧氣比冷水少。"},{"w":"eutrophication","p":"n.","d":"too many nutrients in water, which causes plants to grow too much","c":"優養化","s":"eutrophication happens when too many nutrients enter the water, so the lake turns green and fish begin to die.","t":"當太多養分進入水中時就會發生優養化,所以湖水變綠,魚也開始死亡。"},{"w":"algal bloom","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fast increase of algae in water","c":"藻華","s":"An algal bloom turned the water bright green, and the government closed the beach because the water was unsafe.","t":"藻華讓海水變成鮮綠色,而政府關閉了海灘,因為海水不安全。"},{"w":"red tide","p":"n.phr.","d":"a harmful algae bloom that makes the sea look red","c":"赤潮;紅潮","s":"Shellfish from the area were banned during the red tide, because eating them could make people seriously ill.","t":"紅潮期間禁止販售該地區的有殼海鮮,因為吃了可能讓人嚴重生病。"},{"w":"toxin","p":"n.","d":"a poisonous substance made by a living thing","c":"毒素","s":"Some algae produce a toxin that builds up in shellfish, so people can get sick even when the seafood looks fresh.","t":"有些藻類會產生在貝類體內累積的毒素,所以即使海鮮看起來很新鮮,人們還是可能生病。"},{"w":"mercury","p":"n.","d":"a poisonous silver metal that can build up in fish","c":"汞;水銀","s":"Large fish like tuna may contain mercury, so doctors advise pregnant women to eat them only once in a while.","t":"像鮪魚這樣的大型魚可能含有汞,所以醫生建議孕婦只偶爾吃。"},{"w":"heavy metal","p":"n.phr.","d":"a dangerous metal such as lead or mercury","c":"重金屬","s":"A heavy metal like lead can stay in the sea for a long time, and it slowly builds up in the bodies of marine animals.","t":"像鉛這樣的重金屬能在海中停留很久,而且它會慢慢在海洋動物體內累積。"},{"w":"noise pollution","p":"n.phr.","d":"harmful or annoying levels of noise","c":"噪音污染","s":"Ships create a lot of noise pollution underwater, so whales find it harder to hear each other over long distances.","t":"船隻在水下製造大量噪音污染,所以鯨魚更難在遠距離聽到彼此。"},{"w":"discharge","p":"v.","d":"to let a liquid or gas flow out","c":"排放","s":"Factories are not allowed to discharge hot water into the bay, because sudden warming can kill coral and fish.","t":"工廠不准把熱水排放到海灣中,因為突然升溫會殺死珊瑚和魚類。"},{"w":"dredge","p":"v.","d":"to dig mud and sand from the bottom of a river, harbour or sea","c":"疏浚;挖泥","s":"The port plans to dredge the harbour to let bigger ships in, but environmental groups say it will destroy seagrass.","t":"港務單位計畫疏浚港口讓更大的船隻進入,但環保團體說這會破壞海草。"},{"w":"ballast water","p":"n.phr.","d":"sea water carried in a ship to keep it steady","c":"壓艙水","s":"Ships carry ballast water from one country to another, so tiny foreign animals can be released into new seas.","t":"船隻把壓艙水從一個國家帶到另一個國家,所以微小的外來生物可能被釋放到新的海域。"},{"w":"pathogen","p":"n.","d":"a very small living thing that causes disease","c":"病原體","s":"A new pathogen has killed many starfish along the coast, and scientists think warmer water helped it spread.","t":"一種新的病原體已經殺死沿岸許多海星,而科學家認為較溫暖的海水幫助它擴散。"},{"w":"single-use","p":"adj.","d":"made to be used once and then thrown away","c":"一次性的","s":"Our school stopped selling drinks in single-use bottles, and students now bring their own water bottles every day.","t":"我們學校停止販售一次性瓶裝飲料,而學生們現在每天自己帶水瓶。"},{"w":"straw","p":"n.","d":"a thin tube used for drinking","c":"吸管","s":"Many cafés in Taipei have stopped giving out a plastic straw with each drink, so customers use paper or metal ones instead.","t":"台北許多咖啡店已經不再每杯飲料附上塑膠吸管,所以顧客改用紙製或金屬吸管。"},{"w":"packaging","p":"n.","d":"the materials used to wrap or protect goods","c":"包裝","s":"Online shopping creates a lot of packaging, and much of this plastic ends up in rivers and then the sea.","t":"網路購物產生大量包裝,而這些塑膠很多最後流入河川,然後進入海洋。"},{"w":"biodegradable","p":"adj.","d":"able to break down naturally without harming nature","c":"可生物分解的","s":"The shop uses biodegradable bags made from corn, so they break down naturally instead of polluting the ocean.","t":"這家店使用玉米製成的可生物分解袋子,所以它們會自然分解,而不會污染海洋。"},{"w":"degrade","p":"v.","d":"to break down slowly into smaller parts","c":"分解;降解","s":"Plastic bottles take hundreds of years to degrade, so the ones we throw away today will still be in the sea in 2400.","t":"塑膠瓶需要數百年才能分解,所以我們今天丟掉的瓶子到了2400年仍會在海中。"},{"w":"ingest","p":"v.","d":"to take food or other things into the body","c":"攝入;吞食","s":"Turtles often ingest plastic bags by mistake, because the bags look like jellyfish floating in the water.","t":"海龜常常誤吞塑膠袋,因為袋子看起來就像漂浮在水中的水母。"},{"w":"suffocate","p":"v.","d":"to die because there is no air or oxygen","c":"窒息","s":"Fish suffocate when there is too little oxygen in the water, and thousands may wash up on the beach at once.","t":"當水中氧氣太少時,魚會窒息,而且可能一次有數千條被沖上海灘。"},{"w":"choke","p":"v.","d":"to be unable to breathe because something blocks the throat","c":"噎住;嗆住","s":"Seabirds can choke on bottle caps, because they mistake the bright plastic for small fish.","t":"海鳥可能被瓶蓋噎住,因為牠們把鮮豔的塑膠誤認為小魚。"},{"w":"carcass","p":"n.","d":"the dead body of an animal","c":"屍體(動物)","s":"A whale carcass washed up on the beach last week, and scientists found more than twenty kilograms of plastic in its stomach.","t":"上週一具鯨魚屍體被沖上海灘,而科學家在牠的胃裡發現超過二十公斤的塑膠。"},{"w":"strand","p":"v.","d":"to leave a sea animal stuck on land and unable to return","c":"使擱淺","s":"Low tides sometimes strand dolphins on the beach, so local volunteers keep them wet until the water returns.","t":"退潮有時會使海豚擱淺在海灘上,所以當地志工會讓牠們保持濕潤,直到海水回來。"},{"w":"disposable","p":"adj.","d":"made to be thrown away after use","c":"拋棄式的;用完即丟的","s":"disposable chopsticks and cups are convenient, but they create mountains of waste that often end up in the sea.","t":"免洗筷子和杯子很方便,但它們製造了堆積如山的垃圾,而這些垃圾常常最後流入大海。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Fishing, Shipping & Ocean Resources 漁業、航運與海洋資源","cards":[{"w":"fishery","p":"n.","d":"an area or business where fish are caught","c":"漁場;漁業","s":"The local fishery closed for three months, so fish numbers could recover after years of heavy fishing.","t":"當地漁場關閉三個月,好讓魚群數量在多年的大量捕撈後得以恢復。"},{"w":"fisherman","p":"n.","d":"a person who catches fish as a job","c":"漁夫;漁民","s":"My grandfather was a fisherman for forty years, and he says there were far more fish in the sea when he was young.","t":"我爺爺當了四十年的漁夫,而他說他年輕時海裡的魚多得多。"},{"w":"trawler","p":"n.","d":"a large fishing boat that pulls a big net","c":"拖網漁船","s":"A huge trawler can catch tons of fish in one day, but it also catches many animals that nobody wants to eat.","t":"一艘巨大的拖網漁船一天就能捕到好幾噸的魚,但它也捕到許多沒人想吃的動物。"},{"w":"trawl","p":"v.","d":"to catch fish by pulling a large net through the water","c":"拖網捕魚","s":"Boats that trawl along the sea floor damage coral and sponges, so some countries have banned this method.","t":"沿著海床拖網捕魚的船隻會破壞珊瑚和海綿,所以一些國家已經禁止這種方法。"},{"w":"longline","p":"n.","d":"a very long fishing line with thousands of hooks","c":"延繩釣","s":"A single longline can stretch for many kilometres, and sea turtles and birds are sometimes caught on its hooks.","t":"一條延繩釣可以延伸好幾公里,而且海龜和海鳥有時會被它的鉤子鉤住。"},{"w":"catch","p":"v.","d":"to get hold of a fish or animal","c":"捕捉;抓到","s":"My father caught three large fish yesterday, but he let the smallest one go because it was too young.","t":"我爸爸昨天捕到三條大魚,但他把最小的那條放走了,因為牠太小了。"},{"w":"fish stock","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of fish of one kind in an area","c":"魚類資源;魚群存量","s":"The fish stock of tuna has fallen sharply, so the government has limited how many fish each boat can catch.","t":"鮪魚的魚群存量已經大幅下降,所以政府限制了每艘船能捕撈的魚量。"},{"w":"aquaculture","p":"n.","d":"the farming of fish and other sea creatures","c":"水產養殖","s":"aquaculture provides about half of the seafood we eat today, but badly run farms can pollute the water nearby.","t":"水產養殖提供了我們今天所吃海鮮的大約一半,但管理不善的養殖場會污染附近的水域。"},{"w":"fish farm","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where fish are raised for food","c":"養魚場","s":"The fish farm near our village raises milkfish, and it sells them to restaurants all over southern Taiwan.","t":"我們村子附近的養魚場養殖虱目魚,而且把牠們賣給台灣南部各地的餐廳。"},{"w":"seafood","p":"n.","d":"fish and shellfish eaten as food","c":"海鮮","s":"We had fresh seafood at the night market, and my brother tried grilled squid for the first time.","t":"我們在夜市吃了新鮮的海鮮,而我弟弟第一次嚐試了烤魷魚。"},{"w":"tuna","p":"n.","d":"a large sea fish often eaten in sushi or from cans","c":"鮪魚","s":"Bluefin tuna is very popular in sushi restaurants, but its numbers dropped sharply because of overfishing.","t":"黑鮪魚在壽司店非常受歡迎,但牠的數量因為過度捕撈而大幅減少。"},{"w":"salmon","p":"n.","d":"a fish with pink flesh that swims from the sea up rivers to lay eggs","c":"鮭魚","s":"Every autumn, salmon swim up rivers to lay their eggs, and bears wait by the water to catch them.","t":"每年秋天,鮭魚會逆流而上產卵,而熊會在水邊等著抓牠們。"},{"w":"shrimp","p":"n.","d":"a small sea animal with a shell that people eat","c":"蝦子","s":"Mangroves are often cut down to build shrimp farms, so coastlines lose their natural protection from storms.","t":"紅樹林常被砍伐來興建蝦場,所以海岸線失去了抵擋暴風的天然屏障。"},{"w":"port","p":"n.","d":"a town or city with a harbour where ships load and unload","c":"港口;港市","s":"Kaohsiung is a busy port, and huge ships arrive there every day from all over the world.","t":"高雄是個繁忙的港口,而巨大的船隻每天從世界各地抵達那裡。"},{"w":"cargo","p":"n.","d":"goods carried by a ship, plane or truck","c":"貨物","s":"The ship was carrying cargo from China to Europe, but a storm forced it to stop in Singapore.","t":"這艘船正把貨物從中國運往歐洲,但一場暴風雨迫使它停靠新加坡。"},{"w":"container ship","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large ship that carries goods in big metal boxes","c":"貨櫃船","s":"A container ship got stuck in the Suez Canal in 2021, and hundreds of other ships had to wait for days.","t":"2021年一艘貨櫃船卡在蘇伊士運河,而數百艘其他船隻必須等好幾天。"},{"w":"tanker","p":"n.","d":"a ship that carries oil or other liquids","c":"油輪","s":"The oil tanker ran into rocks near the coast, so thousands of tonnes of oil leaked into the sea.","t":"那艘油輪在海岸附近撞上岩石,所以數千噸的石油漏入海中。"},{"w":"freight","p":"n.","d":"goods carried by ship, train or plane","c":"貨運;貨物","s":"Most international freight travels by sea because it is cheaper, although air transport is much faster.","t":"大部分國際貨運走海運,因為比較便宜,雖然空運快得多。"},{"w":"shipping lane","p":"n.phr.","d":"a regular route used by ships at sea","c":"航道","s":"The shipping lane passes close to a whale feeding area, so ships are asked to slow down during certain months.","t":"這條航道靠近鯨魚的覓食區,所以船隻在某些月份被要求減速。"},{"w":"oil rig","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large structure used to get oil from under the sea","c":"鑽油平台","s":"Workers on the oil rig live at sea for weeks at a time, and they fly home by helicopter.","t":"鑽油平台上的工人一次在海上住好幾週,而且他們搭直升機回家。"},{"w":"drilling","p":"n.","d":"making deep holes in the ground to find oil or gas","c":"鑽探","s":"Offshore drilling brings money to the region, but many residents worry about another oil spill.","t":"離岸鑽探為地區帶來收入,但許多居民擔心再次發生漏油。"},{"w":"mineral","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance such as metal found in rock","c":"礦物","s":"The sea floor contains many valuable mineral, but mining them could destroy habitats that we barely understand.","t":"海床含有許多珍貴的礦物,但開採它們可能會破壞我們幾乎不了解的棲地。"},{"w":"nodule","p":"n.","d":"a small round lump of mineral found on the sea floor","c":"結核(礦物團塊)","s":"Each metal nodule on the sea floor took millions of years to form, so mining companies cannot simply wait for more.","t":"海床上的每一顆金屬結核都花了數百萬年才形成,所以採礦公司無法單純等它再長出來。"},{"w":"wave power","p":"n.phr.","d":"electricity made from the movement of sea waves","c":"波浪發電","s":"Taiwan is surrounded by the sea, so wave power could become an important source of clean energy in the future.","t":"台灣四面環海,所以波浪發電未來可能成為重要的乾淨能源來源。"},{"w":"fishing ground","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area of sea where many fish are caught","c":"漁場","s":"The waters near Penghu are a rich fishing ground, and fishermen there have caught squid for generations.","t":"澎湖附近的海域是豐富的漁場,那裡的漁民世世代代都在捕魷魚。"},{"w":"whaling","p":"n.","d":"the hunting of whales","c":"捕鯨","s":"Most countries have banned whaling, but a few still hunt whales and say it is part of their culture.","t":"大多數國家已經禁止捕鯨,但少數國家仍然獵捕鯨魚,並說這是他們文化的一部分。"},{"w":"harpoon","p":"n.","d":"a long spear used to hunt whales and large fish","c":"魚叉","s":"In the past, hunters threw a harpoon by hand, but modern whaling ships use guns that fire them.","t":"過去,獵人用手投擲魚叉,但現代捕鯨船使用發射魚叉的槍。"},{"w":"bait","p":"n.","d":"food put on a hook or in a trap to catch fish or animals","c":"魚餌;誘餌","s":"We used small pieces of squid as bait, and within ten minutes my sister caught her first fish.","t":"我們用小塊魷魚當魚餌,不到十分鐘我妹妹就釣到她的第一條魚。"},{"w":"overexploit","p":"v.","d":"to use too much of a natural resource so it cannot recover","c":"過度開發;過度利用","s":"If we continue to overexploit the sea, there may be almost no large fish left by the end of this century.","t":"如果我們繼續過度利用海洋,到本世紀末可能幾乎不剩任何大型魚類。"},{"w":"pearl","p":"n.","d":"a small, shiny white ball that grows inside an oyster","c":"珍珠","s":"Each pearl takes years to grow inside an oyster, so natural ones are rare and very expensive.","t":"每一顆珍珠都要在牡蠣裡花好幾年才能長成,所以天然珍珠很稀少且非常昂貴。"},{"w":"coastguard","p":"n.","d":"the organisation that protects people and controls activity along the coast","c":"海巡;海岸巡防隊","s":"The coastguard rescued five fishermen after their boat sank, and they also arrested a ship that was fishing illegally.","t":"海巡在漁船沉沒後救起五名漁民,而且他們也逮捕了一艘非法捕魚的船。"},{"w":"fleet","p":"n.","d":"a group of ships that work together","c":"船隊","s":"The country's fishing fleet has grown to over 2,000 boats, so experts worry that fish cannot reproduce fast enough.","t":"該國的捕魚船隊已經成長到超過兩千艘船,所以專家擔心魚類繁殖的速度跟不上。"},{"w":"fishing net","p":"n.phr.","d":"a net used for catching fish","c":"漁網","s":"An old fishing net was stuck on the reef, and the divers spent an hour cutting it free.","t":"一張舊漁網卡在珊瑚礁上,潛水員們花了一個小時把它割下來。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (abundance – designate)","cards":[{"w":"abundance","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of something","c":"豐富;大量","s":"There is an abundance of fish around the protected reef, so local divers earn more money from tourists than before.","t":"受保護的珊瑚礁周圍有大量的魚,所以當地潛水員從遊客身上賺的錢比以前多。"},{"w":"adhere","p":"v.","d":"to follow a rule or agreement closely","c":"遵守;堅持","s":"All boats must adhere to the new speed limits in the bay, or they will have to pay a heavy fine.","t":"所有船隻都必須遵守海灣新的速限,否則將被處以重罰。"},{"w":"advent","p":"n.","d":"the arrival or beginning of something important","c":"出現;到來","s":"Since the advent of cheap plastic in the 1950s, the amount of rubbish in the ocean has grown every year.","t":"自從1950年代廉價塑膠出現以來,海洋中的垃圾量每年都在增加。"},{"w":"ample","p":"adj.","d":"more than enough","c":"充足的;大量的","s":"The research ship carries ample food and fuel for two months, so the scientists do not need to return to port often.","t":"研究船載有足夠兩個月的充足食物和燃料,所以科學家不需要常常返港。"},{"w":"analogous","p":"adj.","d":"similar in some way","c":"類似的","s":"A coral reef is analogous to a busy city, because thousands of different creatures live and work closely together.","t":"珊瑚礁類似一座繁忙的城市,因為成千上萬種不同的生物緊密地一起生活和運作。"},{"w":"apparatus","p":"n.","d":"equipment used for a particular purpose","c":"儀器;設備","s":"Divers must check their breathing apparatus carefully, because one broken part could put their lives in danger.","t":"潛水員必須仔細檢查他們的呼吸設備,因為一個損壞的零件就可能危及生命。"},{"w":"appreciable","p":"adj.","d":"large enough to be noticed","c":"可觀的;明顯的","s":"The ban on plastic bags led to an appreciable drop in beach litter, and volunteers noticed the change within a year.","t":"塑膠袋禁令讓海灘垃圾明顯減少,而志工在一年內就注意到這個改變。"},{"w":"audit","p":"n.","d":"an official check of records or activities","c":"稽核;審查","s":"The government carried out an audit of all fishing boats, and it found that some were catching more than allowed.","t":"政府對所有漁船進行稽核,並發現有些船的捕撈量超過規定。"},{"w":"autonomy","p":"n.","d":"the freedom to make your own decisions","c":"自主權","s":"Local fishing villages want more autonomy over their waters, because they understand the sea better than officials in the city.","t":"當地漁村希望對自己的水域有更多自主權,因為他們比城市裡的官員更了解大海。"},{"w":"cater","p":"v.","d":"to provide what people need or want","c":"迎合;滿足需求","s":"The aquarium has special tours that cater to young children, so families with toddlers can enjoy the visit too.","t":"水族館有專門迎合幼童的導覽,所以有幼兒的家庭也能享受參觀。"},{"w":"compel","p":"v.","d":"to force someone to do something","c":"迫使;強迫","s":"Rising fuel prices compel many fishermen to stay in port, so fresh seafood became more expensive at the market.","t":"上漲的油價迫使許多漁民留在港內,所以市場上的新鮮海鮮變得更貴。"},{"w":"conducive","p":"adj.","d":"helping something to happen","c":"有助於……的","s":"Warm, clear water is conducive to coral growth, but water that is too hot can kill the reef.","t":"溫暖清澈的海水有助於珊瑚生長,但太熱的海水會殺死珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"confer","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something with others before deciding","c":"商議;協商","s":"The ship's captain had to confer with the coastguard before he changed course, because the weather was getting worse.","t":"船長在改變航向前必須與海巡商議,因為天氣越來越糟。"},{"w":"configuration","p":"n.","d":"the way parts are arranged","c":"配置;結構","s":"The configuration of the new offshore wind farm was changed, so the turbines would not block the whales' route.","t":"新離岸風場的配置被修改了,這樣風機就不會擋住鯨魚的路線。"},{"w":"consecutive","p":"adj.","d":"following one after another without a break","c":"連續的","s":"The reef has suffered from very hot water for three consecutive summers, so scientists fear it may not recover.","t":"這片珊瑚礁已經連續三個夏天受到極熱海水的影響,所以科學家擔心它可能無法恢復。"},{"w":"constituent","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that form something","c":"成分;組成部分","s":"Salt is the main constituent that makes sea water different from river water, but it also contains many other minerals.","t":"鹽是讓海水與河水不同的主要成分,但海水也含有許多其他礦物質。"},{"w":"contemplate","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"考慮;沉思","s":"The town is contemplate a ban on jet skis near the beach, because the noise disturbs both swimmers and dolphins.","t":"鎮上正在考慮禁止在海灘附近使用水上摩托車,因為噪音會干擾泳客和海豚。"},{"w":"contingent","p":"adj.","d":"depending on something else","c":"取決於……的","s":"Our boat trip is contingent on the weather, so we will check the forecast tomorrow morning before we decide.","t":"我們的乘船行程取決於天氣,所以我們明天早上決定前會先看天氣預報。"},{"w":"convene","p":"v.","d":"to come together for a formal meeting","c":"召開;召集","s":"World leaders will convene in New York next month, and they hope to sign a treaty to protect the high seas.","t":"世界領袖下個月將在紐約召開會議,而他們希望簽署一項保護公海的條約。"},{"w":"curtail","p":"v.","d":"to reduce or limit something","c":"削減;限制","s":"The government decided to curtail fishing during the spawning season, so the fish could lay their eggs safely.","t":"政府決定在產卵季節限制捕魚,讓魚能安全地產卵。"},{"w":"dedicate","p":"v.","d":"to give your time and energy to something","c":"奉獻;致力於","s":"She has dedicate her life to protecting sea turtles, and she spends every summer guarding their nests at night.","t":"她把一生奉獻給保護海龜,而且她每年夏天晚上都在守護牠們的巢。"},{"w":"deliberate","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose","c":"故意的;蓄意的","s":"The oil spill was not an accident but a deliberate act, so the ship's owner was taken to court.","t":"這起漏油不是意外而是蓄意的行為,所以船主被告上法院。"},{"w":"delineate","p":"v.","d":"to describe or mark the exact edges of something","c":"劃定;描繪","s":"The new map clearly delineate the borders of the marine park, so fishermen know exactly where they cannot fish.","t":"新地圖清楚劃定了海洋公園的邊界,所以漁民確切知道哪裡不能捕魚。"},{"w":"denote","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of something","c":"表示;代表","s":"Red flags on the beach denote dangerous currents, so swimmers should stay out of the water when they see them.","t":"海灘上的紅旗表示有危險的海流,所以泳客看到時應該遠離水域。"},{"w":"designate","p":"v.","d":"to officially choose something for a purpose","c":"指定;劃定","s":"The government plans to designate the bay as a protected area, and fishing there will be banned from next year.","t":"政府計畫把這個海灣劃定為保護區,而且明年起將禁止在那裡捕魚。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (devise – optimal)","cards":[{"w":"devise","p":"v.","d":"to plan or invent a new way of doing something","c":"設計;想出","s":"Students devise a simple machine that collects floating plastic, and they tested it in the river near their school.","t":"學生們設計了一台收集漂浮塑膠的簡單機器,而且在學校附近的河裡進行測試。"},{"w":"disperse","p":"v.","d":"to spread over a wide area","c":"分散;擴散","s":"Strong winds helped disperse the oil across a large area, so the clean-up became much more difficult.","t":"強風讓油污擴散到大片區域,所以清理工作變得困難許多。"},{"w":"disrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from continuing normally","c":"擾亂;破壞","s":"Loud ship noise can disrupt the way whales communicate, so they may lose contact with their family groups.","t":"巨大的船隻噪音會擾亂鯨魚的溝通方式,所以牠們可能和家族群體失去聯繫。"},{"w":"dissipate","p":"v.","d":"to slowly disappear or become weaker","c":"消散;消失","s":"The typhoon began to dissipate after it reached land, but heavy rain continued for two more days.","t":"颱風登陸後開始減弱消散,但大雨又持續了兩天。"},{"w":"diverge","p":"v.","d":"to go in different directions","c":"分歧;分開","s":"Scientists' opinions diverge on deep-sea mining, because some focus on the metals while others focus on the damage.","t":"科學家們對深海採礦的看法分歧,因為有些人著重在金屬,而有些人著重在破壞。"},{"w":"divert","p":"v.","d":"to change the direction of something","c":"使改道;轉移","s":"The ship was divert to a different port because of the storm, so the passengers arrived a day late.","t":"這艘船因為暴風雨被改道到另一個港口,所以乘客晚了一天抵達。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"able to last a long time without breaking","c":"耐用的","s":"Fishing nets are made of durable plastic, so they can stay in the ocean for hundreds of years after they are lost.","t":"漁網是用耐用的塑膠製成的,所以遺失後它們能在海洋中留存數百年。"},{"w":"elicit","p":"v.","d":"to get a reaction or information from someone","c":"引出;引起","s":"The photo of a turtle with a straw in its nose elicit a strong reaction online, and many people stopped using straws.","t":"一張海龜鼻子插著吸管的照片在網路上引起強烈反應,而許多人因此不再使用吸管。"},{"w":"elusive","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to find or catch","c":"難以捉摸的;難找到的","s":"The giant squid is so elusive that nobody filmed one alive until 2012, although sailors told stories about it for centuries.","t":"大王魷魚非常難以找到,直到2012年才有人拍到活體,儘管水手們講述牠的故事已經好幾個世紀。"},{"w":"embark","p":"v.","d":"to start something new and important","c":"開始;著手","s":"The team will embark on a two-year study of the reef, and they will dive there every month to collect data.","t":"團隊將著手一項為期兩年的珊瑚礁研究,而且他們每個月都會潛到那裡收集數據。"},{"w":"endeavour","p":"n.","d":"a serious attempt to do something difficult","c":"努力;嘗試","s":"Cleaning the whole ocean is a huge endeavour, but every small action by individuals still makes a difference.","t":"清理整個海洋是一項巨大的努力,但每個人的小行動仍然能帶來改變。"},{"w":"envisage","p":"v.","d":"to imagine something as a future possibility","c":"設想;預見","s":"The mayor envisage a clean harbour where children can swim safely, so she has started a ten-year plan.","t":"市長設想一個孩子們能安全游泳的乾淨港口,所以她已經啟動了一項十年計畫。"},{"w":"exhaustive","p":"adj.","d":"very complete and including everything","c":"詳盡的;徹底的","s":"The report gives an exhaustive list of all the fish species in the bay, and it took researchers five years to finish.","t":"這份報告列出了海灣內所有魚種的詳盡清單,而研究人員花了五年才完成。"},{"w":"formulate","p":"v.","d":"to develop a plan carefully","c":"制定;規劃","s":"The council is trying to formulate a plan to reduce plastic waste, and it wants ideas from local students.","t":"議會正在試著制定減少塑膠垃圾的計畫,而且它希望聽取當地學生的想法。"},{"w":"identical","p":"adj.","d":"exactly the same","c":"完全相同的","s":"The two fish look almost identical, but one lives only in fresh water while the other lives in the sea.","t":"這兩種魚看起來幾乎一模一樣,但一種只生活在淡水中,而另一種生活在海裡。"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large","c":"巨大的;龐大的","s":"The ocean holds an immense amount of heat, so it has slowed down global warming on land.","t":"海洋儲存了巨大的熱量,所以它減緩了陸地上的全球暖化。"},{"w":"imperative","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important and needing urgent action","c":"迫切的;必要的","s":"It is imperative that we protect the remaining mangroves, because they defend the coast and store large amounts of carbon.","t":"保護剩下的紅樹林是刻不容緩的,因為它們保護海岸並儲存大量的碳。"},{"w":"inclination","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that makes you want to do something","c":"傾向;意願","s":"Many young people have little inclination to become fishermen, so the average age of fishermen keeps rising.","t":"許多年輕人沒什麼意願成為漁民,所以漁民的平均年齡持續上升。"},{"w":"intricate","p":"adj.","d":"having many small parts or details","c":"錯綜複雜的;精細的","s":"The intricate shapes of coral provide hiding places for small fish, so a healthy reef supports many kinds of life.","t":"珊瑚錯綜複雜的形狀為小魚提供藏身處,所以健康的珊瑚礁能支持許多種生命。"},{"w":"invaluable","p":"adj.","d":"extremely useful","c":"非常寶貴的","s":"Local fishermen gave invaluable help to the scientists, because they knew exactly where the rare fish could be found.","t":"當地漁民給了科學家非常寶貴的幫助,因為他們確切知道哪裡能找到稀有的魚。"},{"w":"inventory","p":"n.","d":"a complete list of things in a place","c":"清單;盤點","s":"Divers made an inventory of every coral species on the reef, so they could see changes in the following years.","t":"潛水員為珊瑚礁上的每一種珊瑚做了清單,這樣他們就能看到接下來幾年的變化。"},{"w":"legitimate","p":"adj.","d":"fair, reasonable or legal","c":"合理的;合法的","s":"Fishermen have legitimate concerns about the new rules, because their families depend on fishing for income.","t":"漁民對新規定有合理的擔憂,因為他們的家庭依靠捕魚維生。"},{"w":"numerous","p":"adj.","d":"many","c":"許多的;眾多的","s":"The beach clean-up found numerous bottle caps and lighters, and many of them had come from other countries.","t":"淨灘活動發現了許多瓶蓋和打火機,而它們有很多來自其他國家。"},{"w":"omit","p":"v.","d":"to leave out something","c":"省略;遺漏","s":"The company omit important facts about the oil leak in its report, so the public did not trust its explanation.","t":"公司在報告中遺漏了漏油的重要事實,所以大眾不相信它的解釋。"},{"w":"optimal","p":"adj.","d":"best or most suitable","c":"最佳的","s":"Early morning is the optimal time for diving here, because the water is calm and the light is soft.","t":"清晨是這裡潛水的最佳時間,因為海水平靜而且光線柔和。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (orient – circumvent)","cards":[{"w":"orient","p":"v.","d":"to find your position or direction","c":"定向;確定方位","s":"Sea turtles use the Earth's magnetic field to orient themselves, so they can return to the beach where they were born.","t":"海龜利用地球的磁場來定向,所以牠們能回到出生的海灘。"},{"w":"pertinent","p":"adj.","d":"directly connected to the subject","c":"相關的;切題的","s":"The student asked a pertinent question about plastic in seafood, and the expert was happy to explain the latest research.","t":"那位學生問了一個關於海鮮中塑膠的切題問題,而專家很樂意解釋最新的研究。"},{"w":"practitioner","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a skilled job","c":"從業人員;實踐者","s":"Every diving practitioner must complete safety training, because guiding tourists underwater is a serious responsibility.","t":"每位潛水從業人員都必須完成安全訓練,因為在水下帶領遊客是一項重大的責任。"},{"w":"prone","p":"adj.","d":"likely to suffer from something","c":"易於……的","s":"This part of the coast is prone to strong currents, so swimming is not allowed without a lifeguard.","t":"這段海岸容易出現強勁的海流,所以沒有救生員時禁止游泳。"},{"w":"provoke","p":"v.","d":"to cause a strong reaction","c":"引起;激起","s":"The plan to build a factory near the reef provoke angry protests, and thousands of people signed a petition against it.","t":"在珊瑚礁附近興建工廠的計畫引起憤怒的抗議,而且數千人連署反對。"},{"w":"proximity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being near","c":"鄰近;接近","s":"Because of its proximity to the sea, the town has fresh seafood, but it also faces greater danger from typhoons.","t":"由於鄰近大海,這個小鎮有新鮮的海鮮,但它也面臨更大的颱風威脅。"},{"w":"readily","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and easily","c":"容易地;迅速地","s":"Plastic bags are readily available in many shops, so people use them without thinking about where they end up.","t":"塑膠袋在許多商店都很容易取得,所以人們使用時不會去想它們最後的去處。"},{"w":"recede","p":"v.","d":"to move back from a higher point","c":"退去;後退","s":"After the storm, the water began to recede, and people returned to clean the mud from their homes.","t":"暴風雨過後,海水開始退去,人們回去清理家中的泥巴。"},{"w":"reciprocal","p":"adj.","d":"given or done in return by both sides","c":"互惠的;相互的","s":"The two countries signed a reciprocal agreement, so each one can fish in the other's waters under strict rules.","t":"兩國簽訂了一項互惠協議,所以雙方都能在嚴格規定下在對方水域捕魚。"},{"w":"regenerate","p":"v.","d":"to grow again after damage","c":"再生;重新生長","s":"A starfish can regenerate a lost arm, but it takes several months for the new arm to grow fully.","t":"海星能再生失去的觸腕,但新的觸腕要好幾個月才能完全長好。"},{"w":"render","p":"v.","d":"to cause something to be in a certain condition","c":"使成為;使變得","s":"The oil spill render the beach unsafe for months, so many hotels lost most of their summer guests.","t":"漏油使海灘好幾個月都不安全,所以許多飯店失去了大部分夏季客人。"},{"w":"replenish","p":"v.","d":"to fill something up again","c":"補充;使恢復","s":"Fish need time to replenish their numbers, so the fishing season is closed for three months every year.","t":"魚類需要時間來恢復數量,所以每年漁季會關閉三個月。"},{"w":"reproduce","p":"v.","d":"to produce young animals or plants","c":"繁殖","s":"Many sharks reproduce slowly and have only a few babies, so their numbers fall quickly when too many are caught.","t":"許多鯊魚繁殖緩慢,而且只生幾隻寶寶,所以捕撈太多時牠們的數量會快速下降。"},{"w":"restrain","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from doing something","c":"抑制;克制","s":"Parents should restrain their children from touching coral, because even a gentle touch can damage the living animals.","t":"父母應該制止孩子觸摸珊瑚,因為即使輕輕一碰也可能傷害這些活的生物。"},{"w":"segment","p":"n.","d":"one part of something","c":"部分;區段","s":"Only one segment of the coast is open to tourists, while the rest is protected for nesting birds.","t":"海岸只有一個區段開放給遊客,而其餘部分是為了築巢的鳥類而受到保護。"},{"w":"sparse","p":"adj.","d":"small in number and spread out","c":"稀疏的;稀少的","s":"Fish are sparse in the open ocean far from land, but they gather in large numbers near reefs and coasts.","t":"遠離陸地的大洋中魚類稀少,但牠們會大量聚集在珊瑚礁和海岸附近。"},{"w":"subtle","p":"adj.","d":"small and not easy to notice","c":"細微的;微妙的","s":"The changes in the reef were subtle at first, but after five years most of the colourful coral had disappeared.","t":"珊瑚礁的變化起初很細微,但五年後大部分色彩繽紛的珊瑚都消失了。"},{"w":"surplus","p":"n.","d":"an amount that is more than needed","c":"過剩;剩餘","s":"The fish farm produced a surplus this year, so the owner gave extra fish to a local food bank.","t":"今年養魚場的產量過剩,所以老闆把多出來的魚送給當地的食物銀行。"},{"w":"abrupt","p":"adj.","d":"sudden and unexpected","c":"突然的","s":"There was an abrupt drop in water temperature, and many tropical fish died because they could not adjust in time.","t":"水溫突然下降,許多熱帶魚因為無法及時適應而死亡。"},{"w":"aesthetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with beauty","c":"美學的;審美的","s":"The coastline has great aesthetic value, so people are against building a large factory that would spoil the view.","t":"這條海岸線有極高的美學價值,所以人們反對興建會破壞景觀的大型工廠。"},{"w":"align","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things so they agree or match","c":"使一致;使對齊","s":"The new fishing rules align with international law, so Taiwanese boats can continue to sell fish to Europe.","t":"新的漁業規定與國際法一致,所以台灣的船隻能繼續把魚賣到歐洲。"},{"w":"aspire","p":"v.","d":"to have a strong wish to achieve something","c":"渴望;立志","s":"Many students aspire to work in marine science, but they need strong maths and biology skills first.","t":"許多學生立志從事海洋科學工作,但他們首先需要很好的數學和生物能力。"},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone confidently that something is true","c":"向……保證","s":"The captain assure the passengers that the storm would pass soon, and he asked them to stay inside.","t":"船長向乘客保證暴風雨很快就會過去,並請他們待在室內。"},{"w":"authentic","p":"adj.","d":"real and not a copy","c":"真正的;道地的","s":"The restaurant serves authentic fishermen's dishes, and the owner buys fresh fish from the harbour every morning.","t":"這家餐廳供應道地的漁家料理,而老闆每天早上都從港口買新鮮的魚。"},{"w":"circumvent","p":"v.","d":"to find a way around a rule or problem","c":"規避;繞過","s":"Some fishing boats circumvent the rules by changing their flags, so it is hard for officials to track them.","t":"有些漁船藉由更換船旗來規避規定,所以官員很難追蹤它們。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (culminate – affluent)","cards":[{"w":"culminate","p":"v.","d":"to end with an important event","c":"以……告終;達到頂點","s":"Years of protests culminate in a new law that banned plastic bags, and many people saw it as a great victory.","t":"多年的抗議最終促成一項禁用塑膠袋的新法律,而許多人把它視為一大勝利。"},{"w":"decisive","p":"adj.","d":"having a very important effect on the result","c":"決定性的","s":"Quick action by the coastguard played a decisive role, because the oil was stopped before it reached the beach.","t":"海巡的迅速行動發揮了決定性的作用,因為油污在抵達海灘前就被攔住了。"},{"w":"disclose","p":"v.","d":"to make information known to the public","c":"揭露;公開","s":"The company refused to disclose how much waste it had dumped into the sea, so journalists began their own investigation.","t":"公司拒絕公開它把多少廢棄物傾倒入海,所以記者們開始自行調查。"},{"w":"empower","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the power or confidence to do something","c":"賦予……權力;使有能力","s":"The project empower local villagers to manage their own fishing areas, and fish numbers have since increased.","t":"這個計畫賦予當地村民管理自己漁區的權力,而魚群數量從那時起就增加了。"},{"w":"equip","p":"v.","d":"to provide the tools needed for a job","c":"配備;裝備","s":"The new research boat is equip with modern sonar, so scientists can map the sea floor in great detail.","t":"新的研究船配備有現代聲納,所以科學家能非常詳細地繪製海床地圖。"},{"w":"expertise","p":"n.","d":"special skill or knowledge","c":"專業知識;專長","s":"The team needed someone with expertise in underwater filming, so they hired a famous wildlife cameraman.","t":"團隊需要一位具備水下攝影專業的人,所以他們聘請了一位知名的野生動物攝影師。"},{"w":"incident","p":"n.","d":"an event, especially an unusual or unpleasant one","c":"事件;事故","s":"The shark incident frightened many tourists, but experts reminded everyone that attacks are extremely rare.","t":"這起鯊魚事件嚇壞了許多遊客,但專家提醒大家攻擊事件極為罕見。"},{"w":"insert","p":"v.","d":"to put something inside something else","c":"插入;放入","s":"Scientists insert a tiny tracker under the turtle's shell, and now they can follow its journey across the ocean.","t":"科學家在海龜的殼下放入一個微小的追蹤器,現在他們能追蹤牠橫越海洋的旅程。"},{"w":"instruct","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone officially what to do","c":"指示;教導","s":"The guide instruct us not to touch anything underwater, because some sea creatures can sting or bite.","t":"導遊指示我們不要碰水下的任何東西,因為有些海洋生物會螫人或咬人。"},{"w":"medium","p":"n.","d":"a way of communicating or expressing something","c":"媒介;媒體","s":"Film is a powerful medium for teaching people about the ocean, because many viewers have never seen a coral reef.","t":"影片是教導人們認識海洋的強大媒介,因為許多觀眾從未見過珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"mode","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of doing something","c":"方式;模式","s":"Shipping is the cheapest mode of transport for heavy goods, but it also produces a lot of pollution.","t":"海運是運送重物最便宜的運輸方式,但它也產生大量污染。"},{"w":"panel","p":"n.","d":"a group of experts who discuss or decide something","c":"小組;委員會","s":"A panel of scientists will review the mining plan, and their report will be shared with the public next month.","t":"一個科學家小組將審查採礦計畫,而他們的報告下個月會公開。"},{"w":"prime","p":"adj.","d":"main or most important","c":"主要的;首要的","s":"Overfishing is a prime cause of the decline in shark numbers, but climate change also plays a part.","t":"過度捕撈是鯊魚數量下降的主要原因,但氣候變遷也有影響。"},{"w":"principal","p":"adj.","d":"most important","c":"主要的","s":"Tourism is the island's principal source of income, so a healthy reef is important for every family there.","t":"觀光業是這座島的主要收入來源,所以健康的珊瑚礁對那裡的每個家庭都很重要。"},{"w":"transit","p":"n.","d":"the act of moving people or goods from one place to another","c":"運輸;運送","s":"Some fish die during transit to the market, so fishermen keep them in cold water on the boat.","t":"有些魚在運送到市場的途中死亡,所以漁民在船上把牠們養在冷水中。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"an idea or hope about the future","c":"願景;遠見","s":"The organisation has a vision of plastic-free oceans by 2050, but it knows the goal will be very hard to reach.","t":"這個組織有一個在2050年前實現無塑海洋的願景,但它知道這個目標非常難達成。"},{"w":"involve","p":"v.","d":"to include someone or something as a necessary part","c":"涉及;使參與","s":"The clean-up project will involve students from ten schools, and each class will look after one part of the beach.","t":"淨灘計畫將讓十所學校的學生參與,而每個班級將負責海灘的一部分。"},{"w":"respond","p":"v.","d":"to react to something","c":"回應;反應","s":"Corals respond to heat stress by losing their colour, and they may die if the water does not cool down.","t":"珊瑚會以失去顏色來回應熱壓力,而且如果海水不降溫,它們可能會死亡。"},{"w":"remove","p":"v.","d":"to take something away","c":"移除;去除","s":"Divers worked for three days to remove a huge fishing net, and they freed several trapped turtles.","t":"潛水員花了三天移除一張巨大的漁網,並解救了幾隻受困的海龜。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"something built from many parts","c":"結構;構造","s":"An old oil platform can become a structure for marine life, because coral and fish quickly settle on its legs.","t":"一座舊的鑽油平台可以成為海洋生物的構造物,因為珊瑚和魚很快就會在它的支柱上定居。"},{"w":"export","p":"v.","d":"to sell goods to another country","c":"出口","s":"Taiwan export large amounts of frozen fish every year, and much of it goes to Japan and the United States.","t":"台灣每年出口大量冷凍魚,而其中很多銷往日本和美國。"},{"w":"index","p":"n.","d":"a number used to measure changes","c":"指數;指標","s":"The ocean health index gives each country a score, so we can compare how well they protect their seas.","t":"海洋健康指數給每個國家一個分數,所以我們能比較它們保護海洋的成效。"},{"w":"licence","p":"n.","d":"an official document that allows you to do something","c":"執照;許可證","s":"You need a fishing licence to fish in this lake, and the money helps pay for protecting the fish.","t":"在這座湖釣魚需要釣魚許可證,而這筆錢有助於支付保護魚類的費用。"},{"w":"error","p":"n.","d":"a mistake","c":"錯誤","s":"A small error in the ship's map led it onto the rocks, so the company now checks all its maps twice.","t":"船上地圖的一個小錯誤導致它撞上礁石,所以公司現在會把所有地圖檢查兩次。"},{"w":"affluent","p":"adj.","d":"rich and having a comfortable life","c":"富裕的","s":"affluent countries eat far more seafood per person, but poorer coastal communities often depend on fish to survive.","t":"富裕國家每人吃的海鮮多得多,但較貧窮的沿海社區常常依賴魚類維生。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (amenity – discourse)","cards":[{"w":"amenity","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a place comfortable or easy to use","c":"便利設施","s":"The new beach park has every amenity visitors need, such as showers and toilets, but it also has strict rules about rubbish.","t":"新的海灘公園有遊客需要的各種便利設施,例如淋浴間和廁所,但它對垃圾也有嚴格的規定。"},{"w":"anecdotal","p":"adj.","d":"based on personal stories, not careful research","c":"傳聞的;軼事的","s":"Fishermen have anecdotal evidence that fish are getting smaller, but scientists want more data before they agree.","t":"漁民有魚越來越小的傳聞證據,但科學家在同意之前想要更多數據。"},{"w":"apathy","p":"n.","d":"a lack of interest or concern","c":"冷漠;漠不關心","s":"Public apathy about ocean pollution is a big problem, because people rarely see what happens under the waves.","t":"大眾對海洋污染的冷漠是個大問題,因為人們很少看到海浪下發生的事。"},{"w":"arduous","p":"adj.","d":"very difficult and tiring","c":"艱鉅的;費力的","s":"Rowing across the Atlantic is an arduous journey, and the young woman spent ninety days alone on the ocean.","t":"划船橫越大西洋是一段艱辛的旅程,而那位年輕女子獨自在海上度過了九十天。"},{"w":"attest","p":"v.","d":"to show or prove that something is true","c":"證明;證實","s":"Local divers can attest to the reef's recovery, because they have seen the fish return over the past few years.","t":"當地潛水員能證明珊瑚礁的恢復,因為他們這幾年親眼看到魚群回來。"},{"w":"authorise","p":"v.","d":"to give official permission for something","c":"授權;批准","s":"Only the government can authorise fishing in the marine park, and boats without permits will be stopped.","t":"只有政府能批准在海洋公園內捕魚,而沒有許可證的船隻將被攔下。"},{"w":"avert","p":"v.","d":"to prevent something bad from happening","c":"避免;防止","s":"Quick action by the crew helped avert a disaster, because they fixed the leak before the ship began to sink.","t":"船員的迅速行動幫助避免了一場災難,因為他們在船開始下沉前修好了漏洞。"},{"w":"bleak","p":"adj.","d":"without hope or encouragement","c":"黯淡的;無望的","s":"The future of the reef looks bleak if sea temperatures keep rising, but scientists say it is not too late to act.","t":"如果海水溫度持續上升,珊瑚礁的前景看起來很黯淡,但科學家說現在採取行動還不算太遲。"},{"w":"breakthrough","p":"n.","d":"an important new discovery","c":"突破","s":"Scientists made a breakthrough in growing coral in labs, so damaged reefs may be repaired faster in the future.","t":"科學家在實驗室培育珊瑚方面取得了突破,所以受損的珊瑚礁未來可能會更快被修復。"},{"w":"burgeoning","p":"adj.","d":"growing quickly","c":"迅速發展的","s":"The island's burgeoning diving industry has created many jobs, but it also puts more pressure on the reefs.","t":"這座島迅速發展的潛水產業創造了許多工作機會,但它也對珊瑚礁造成更大的壓力。"},{"w":"capitalise","p":"v.","d":"to use a situation to gain an advantage","c":"利用;從中獲利","s":"The town decided to capitalise on its whale-watching tours, and tourism has now replaced fishing as its main business.","t":"這個小鎮決定利用賞鯨行程,而觀光業現在已經取代捕魚成為它的主要產業。"},{"w":"catalyst","p":"n.","d":"something that causes an important change","c":"催化劑;促成因素","s":"The oil spill was a catalyst for change, because it made the public demand stricter safety laws for ships.","t":"這起漏油事件是改變的催化劑,因為它讓大眾要求更嚴格的船舶安全法規。"},{"w":"cautious","p":"adj.","d":"careful to avoid danger","c":"謹慎的;小心的","s":"New divers should be cautious near strong currents, so they should always stay close to their guide.","t":"新手潛水員在強勁海流附近應該謹慎,所以他們應該總是待在導遊身邊。"},{"w":"complacent","p":"adj.","d":"too satisfied and not worried about possible danger","c":"自滿的;掉以輕心的","s":"We cannot become complacent after one good year, because fish numbers can fall again very quickly.","t":"我們不能在一個好年之後就掉以輕心,因為魚群數量可能會很快再次下降。"},{"w":"concise","p":"adj.","d":"short and clear","c":"簡潔的","s":"The guide gave a concise safety talk before the dive, and everyone understood the rules in just five minutes.","t":"導遊在潛水前做了一段簡潔的安全說明,而每個人只花五分鐘就了解規則。"},{"w":"condemn","p":"v.","d":"to say strongly that something is wrong","c":"譴責","s":"Environmental groups condemn the plan to dump waste at sea, and they asked the government to stop it immediately.","t":"環保團體譴責在海上傾倒廢棄物的計畫,並要求政府立即停止。"},{"w":"conscientious","p":"adj.","d":"careful to do things well and correctly","c":"認真的;盡責的","s":"She is a conscientious diver who always picks up rubbish underwater, so her friends call her the reef's guardian.","t":"她是一位盡責的潛水員,總是在水下撿垃圾,所以朋友們稱她為珊瑚礁守護者。"},{"w":"counterpart","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing with the same role in a different place","c":"對應的人或物;同行","s":"Taiwan's coastguard met its Japanese counterpart to discuss illegal fishing, and they agreed to share information.","t":"台灣海巡與日本的對口單位會面討論非法捕魚,而且雙方同意分享資訊。"},{"w":"cynical","p":"adj.","d":"believing people only act for their own benefit","c":"憤世嫉俗的;懷疑的","s":"Some people are cynical about the company's green promises, because it still sells huge amounts of plastic.","t":"有些人對這家公司的環保承諾抱持懷疑的態度,因為它仍然販售大量塑膠。"},{"w":"daunting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried about whether you can succeed","c":"令人卻步的","s":"Cleaning the whole coastline seemed daunting at first, but hundreds of volunteers finished the job in one weekend.","t":"清理整條海岸線起初看起來令人卻步,但數百名志工在一個週末就完成了工作。"},{"w":"dearth","p":"n.","d":"a lack of something","c":"缺乏;不足","s":"There is a dearth of data about the deep sea, so scientists cannot predict how mining will affect it.","t":"關於深海的數據缺乏,所以科學家無法預測採礦會對它造成什麼影響。"},{"w":"decimate","p":"v.","d":"to destroy or kill a large part of something","c":"大量毀滅;大幅減少","s":"Disease has decimate the starfish population along the coast, and the number of sea urchins has grown quickly as a result.","t":"疾病大幅減少了沿岸的海星數量,而海膽的數量因此迅速增加。"},{"w":"demographic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the age, size and structure of a population","c":"人口統計的","s":"demographic changes in fishing villages are worrying, because most young people have moved to the cities for work.","t":"漁村的人口結構變化令人擔憂,因為大部分年輕人都已經搬到城市工作。"},{"w":"diligent","p":"adj.","d":"working hard and carefully","c":"勤奮的;用功的","s":"The diligent students recorded the water temperature every day for a year, and their data helped a university project.","t":"那些勤奮的學生一整年每天記錄水溫,而他們的數據幫助了一項大學研究計畫。"},{"w":"discourse","p":"n.","d":"serious discussion about a subject","c":"論述;討論","s":"Public discourse about the ocean has changed, because more people now see plastic as a serious problem.","t":"關於海洋的公眾討論已經改變,因為現在更多人把塑膠視為嚴重的問題。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (disparity – illuminate)","cards":[{"w":"disparity","p":"n.","d":"a large difference between things","c":"差異;懸殊","s":"There is a large disparity between rich and poor fishermen, because big companies own most of the modern boats.","t":"富有和貧窮的漁民之間存在很大的差距,因為大公司擁有大部分現代化的船隻。"},{"w":"dispel","p":"v.","d":"to make a belief or feeling disappear","c":"消除;驅散","s":"The documentary helped dispel the myth that sharks hunt humans, and many viewers began to support shark protection.","t":"這部紀錄片幫助破除鯊魚會獵捕人類的迷思,而許多觀眾開始支持保護鯊魚。"},{"w":"efficacy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to produce the result you want","c":"效力;功效","s":"Scientists are testing the efficacy of new nets that let turtles escape, and early results look very promising.","t":"科學家正在測試能讓海龜逃脫的新漁網的效果,而初步結果看起來很有希望。"},{"w":"emulate","p":"v.","d":"to try to copy someone because you admire them","c":"效法;仿效","s":"Other countries hope to emulate Palau's success, because its strict ocean laws have helped fish numbers recover.","t":"其他國家希望效法帛琉的成功,因為它嚴格的海洋法律幫助魚群數量恢復。"},{"w":"enduring","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time","c":"持久的;長久的","s":"The old lighthouse is an enduring symbol of the town, and people still love to take photos there.","t":"這座老燈塔是小鎮長久的象徵,而人們至今仍喜歡在那裡拍照。"},{"w":"entrenched","p":"adj.","d":"firmly established and difficult to change","c":"根深蒂固的","s":"Eating shark fin soup is an entrenched tradition at some weddings, so changing people's habits takes time.","t":"在某些婚宴上吃魚翅湯是根深蒂固的傳統,所以改變人們的習慣需要時間。"},{"w":"ephemeral","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only a short time","c":"短暫的","s":"The glowing blue waves are ephemeral, so tourists must visit on the right nights to see them.","t":"發光的藍色海浪很短暫,所以遊客必須在對的夜晚造訪才能看到。"},{"w":"eradicate","p":"v.","d":"to get rid of something completely","c":"根除;消滅","s":"It is almost impossible to eradicate an invasive fish once it spreads, so prevention is the best approach.","t":"外來魚種一旦擴散就幾乎不可能根除,所以預防是最好的方法。"},{"w":"evade","p":"v.","d":"to escape or avoid something","c":"躲避;逃避","s":"The illegal fishing boat tried to evade the coastguard, but it was caught after a two-hour chase.","t":"那艘非法漁船試圖躲避海巡,但在兩小時的追逐後被逮到。"},{"w":"exert","p":"v.","d":"to use power or influence","c":"施加;運用","s":"Big seafood companies exert strong influence on fishing laws, so smaller fishermen often feel ignored.","t":"大型海鮮公司對漁業法規施加強大影響,所以小規模漁民常常覺得被忽略。"},{"w":"extensive","p":"adj.","d":"covering a large area or including a lot","c":"廣泛的;大量的","s":"The typhoon caused extensive damage to the harbour, and many boats will need months of repairs.","t":"颱風對港口造成大範圍的損害,而許多船隻需要好幾個月的修理。"},{"w":"extrapolate","p":"v.","d":"to use known facts to guess about the future","c":"推斷;推算","s":"Scientists extrapolate from current data that the reef could disappear by 2050, although they hope action will change this.","t":"科學家根據目前的數據推斷珊瑚礁可能在2050年前消失,雖然他們希望採取行動能改變這一點。"},{"w":"fabricate","p":"v.","d":"to invent false information to deceive people","c":"捏造;偽造","s":"The company fabricate its fishing records to hide the illegal catch, but inspectors discovered the truth.","t":"這家公司捏造捕撈紀錄來隱瞞非法漁獲,但檢查人員發現了真相。"},{"w":"facet","p":"n.","d":"one part or side of something","c":"方面;面向","s":"Pollution is only one facet of the problem, because overfishing and warming are also harming the ocean.","t":"污染只是問題的一個面向,因為過度捕撈和暖化也在傷害海洋。"},{"w":"fallacy","p":"n.","d":"a false idea that many people believe","c":"謬誤;錯誤觀念","s":"It is a fallacy that the ocean is too big to be harmed, because human activities have already changed it greatly.","t":"認為海洋大到不會受到傷害是一種謬誤,因為人類活動已經大大改變了它。"},{"w":"forge","p":"v.","d":"to build a strong relationship or agreement","c":"建立;打造","s":"The two countries hope to forge a strong partnership to protect the shared sea, and they will meet again next year.","t":"兩國希望建立強大的夥伴關係來保護共有的海域,而他們明年會再次會面。"},{"w":"formidable","p":"adj.","d":"very powerful or difficult","c":"強大的;令人敬畏的","s":"The great white shark is a formidable hunter, but it is now threatened by humans in many parts of the world.","t":"大白鯊是令人敬畏的獵手,但牠現在在世界許多地方受到人類威脅。"},{"w":"frugal","p":"adj.","d":"careful not to waste money or resources","c":"節儉的","s":"Island families have long lived frugal lives, so they rarely waste food, water or fuel.","t":"島上的家庭長久以來過著節儉的生活,所以他們很少浪費食物、水或燃料。"},{"w":"fruitful","p":"adj.","d":"producing good results","c":"富有成果的","s":"The meeting between fishermen and scientists was fruitful, because both sides agreed on a new plan for the bay.","t":"漁民和科學家之間的會議成果豐碩,因為雙方對海灣的新計畫達成共識。"},{"w":"futile","p":"adj.","d":"having no chance of success","c":"徒勞的;無效的","s":"Cleaning the beach may seem futile when new rubbish arrives every day, but it still saves many animals.","t":"當每天都有新垃圾漂來時,清理海灘可能看起來是徒勞的,但它仍然拯救了許多動物。"},{"w":"hamper","p":"v.","d":"to make it difficult for something to happen","c":"妨礙;阻礙","s":"Bad weather hamper the search for the missing fishermen, so the rescue teams had to wait until the wind dropped.","t":"惡劣天氣阻礙了搜尋失蹤漁民的行動,所以救援隊必須等到風勢減弱。"},{"w":"harness","p":"v.","d":"to control and use natural energy","c":"利用(自然力)","s":"Engineers are trying to harness the power of ocean waves, so coastal towns can produce clean electricity.","t":"工程師正在試著利用海浪的力量,讓沿海城鎮能產生乾淨的電力。"},{"w":"heighten","p":"v.","d":"to make a feeling or effect stronger","c":"提高;加強","s":"News about plastic in seafood has heighten public concern, and many shoppers now ask where their fish comes from.","t":"海鮮中含塑膠的新聞提高了大眾的擔憂,而許多購物者現在會詢問他們的魚來自哪裡。"},{"w":"homogeneous","p":"adj.","d":"made of parts that are all the same","c":"同質的;均勻的","s":"A fish farm is a homogeneous environment with only one species, while a wild reef contains hundreds of different ones.","t":"養魚場是只有一個物種的同質環境,而野生珊瑚礁則有數百種不同的物種。"},{"w":"illuminate","p":"v.","d":"to make something clearer or easier to understand","c":"闡明;照亮","s":"The new study helps illuminate how whales communicate, because it recorded their songs over many years.","t":"這項新研究有助於闡明鯨魚如何溝通,因為它記錄了牠們多年來的歌聲。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (impending – prerequisite)","cards":[{"w":"impending","p":"adj.","d":"about to happen, usually something bad","c":"即將發生的","s":"Fishermen rushed back to the harbour because of the impending storm, and the coastguard closed the sea to all boats.","t":"漁民們因為即將來臨的暴風雨趕回港口,而海巡對所有船隻封閉了海域。"},{"w":"impetus","p":"n.","d":"something that encourages an activity to develop","c":"動力;推動力","s":"The photos of dying coral gave new impetus to the campaign, and thousands of people joined in the following month.","t":"垂死珊瑚的照片給了這項運動新的動力,而接下來一個月有數千人加入。"},{"w":"incur","p":"v.","d":"to experience something unpleasant, such as a cost, as a result of an action","c":"招致;承擔","s":"Boats that fish in protected areas will incur heavy fines, and their owners may lose their licences.","t":"在保護區捕魚的船隻將遭受重罰,而且船主可能失去執照。"},{"w":"indiscriminate","p":"adj.","d":"done without careful choice","c":"不加選擇的;濫用的","s":"indiscriminate fishing with huge nets kills dolphins and turtles, so many people now choose seafood with eco-labels.","t":"用巨網不加選擇地捕魚會殺死海豚和海龜,所以現在許多人選擇有環保標章的海鮮。"},{"w":"influx","p":"n.","d":"the arrival of many people or things","c":"湧入","s":"The influx of tourists every summer brings money to the island, but it also creates huge amounts of rubbish.","t":"每年夏天遊客的湧入為島嶼帶來收入,但也製造了大量垃圾。"},{"w":"inhabit","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place","c":"居住於;棲息於","s":"Strange creatures inhabit the deepest parts of the ocean, and many of them have never been seen by humans.","t":"奇特的生物棲息在海洋最深的地方,而其中許多從未被人類見過。"},{"w":"insurmountable","p":"adj.","d":"too great to be dealt with","c":"無法克服的","s":"The problem of ocean plastic is not insurmountable, but it needs cooperation between governments, companies and ordinary people.","t":"海洋塑膠的問題並非無法克服,但它需要政府、企業和一般民眾之間的合作。"},{"w":"intact","p":"adj.","d":"complete and not damaged","c":"完好無缺的","s":"The ship had been underwater for a hundred years, but its wooden hull was still almost intact because of the cold water.","t":"這艘船已經在水下一百年了,但因為海水冰冷,它的木製船身仍幾乎完好無缺。"},{"w":"interdependent","p":"adj.","d":"depending on each other","c":"相互依賴的","s":"All the creatures on a reef are interdependent, so the loss of one species can affect many others.","t":"珊瑚礁上的所有生物都是相互依存的,所以失去一個物種可能會影響許多其他物種。"},{"w":"intrusive","p":"adj.","d":"disturbing in an unwelcome way","c":"侵擾的;打擾人的","s":"Some whale-watching boats get too close, which is intrusive for the whales, so new rules set a minimum distance.","t":"有些賞鯨船靠得太近,這對鯨魚來說是一種打擾,所以新規定設定了最小距離。"},{"w":"lucrative","p":"adj.","d":"producing a lot of money","c":"有利可圖的;賺錢的","s":"Shark fin is a lucrative business for some traders, but it has caused shark numbers to fall all over the world.","t":"魚翅對某些商人來說是利潤豐厚的生意,但它導致全世界的鯊魚數量下降。"},{"w":"meagre","p":"adj.","d":"very small in amount","c":"微薄的;貧乏的","s":"The fishermen's catch was meagre this year, so many families had to find other work to pay their bills.","t":"今年漁民的漁獲很微薄,所以許多家庭必須找其他工作來支付帳單。"},{"w":"momentum","p":"n.","d":"the force that keeps something moving or developing","c":"動力;氣勢","s":"The campaign against plastic straws gained momentum quickly, and soon many restaurants stopped using them.","t":"反塑膠吸管運動迅速獲得動力,很快許多餐廳就不再使用吸管。"},{"w":"myriad","p":"adj.","d":"very many","c":"無數的;大量的","s":"The reef is home to myriad colourful creatures, and every dive shows you something new and surprising.","t":"珊瑚礁是無數色彩繽紛生物的家,而每一次潛水都讓你看見新奇又令人驚喜的東西。"},{"w":"obscure","p":"adj.","d":"not well known","c":"鮮為人知的","s":"The tiny fish was so obscure that it had no common name, but scientists discovered it could clean sick coral.","t":"這種小魚非常鮮為人知,連個俗名都沒有,但科學家發現牠能清潔生病的珊瑚。"},{"w":"opt","p":"v.","d":"to choose one thing instead of another","c":"選擇","s":"More shoppers now opt for fish with eco-labels, so supermarkets have started to sell more of them.","t":"現在更多購物者選擇有環保標章的魚,所以超市已經開始販售更多這類產品。"},{"w":"outweigh","p":"v.","d":"to be greater or more important than something else","c":"超過;比……更重要","s":"The long-term benefits of a marine park outweigh the short-term losses for fishermen, because fish numbers grow outside the park too.","t":"海洋公園的長期效益超過漁民的短期損失,因為公園外的魚群數量也會增加。"},{"w":"overlook","p":"v.","d":"to fail to notice or consider something","c":"忽視;忽略","s":"People often overlook the role of tiny plankton, but these creatures produce much of the oxygen on Earth.","t":"人們常常忽略微小浮游生物的角色,但這些生物製造了地球上大部分的氧氣。"},{"w":"perpetuate","p":"v.","d":"to make something continue, especially something bad","c":"使持續;使延續","s":"Films that show sharks as monsters perpetuate people's fear, so fewer people support protecting them.","t":"把鯊魚描繪成怪物的電影延續了人們的恐懼,所以支持保護牠們的人變少了。"},{"w":"pinpoint","p":"v.","d":"to find or describe something exactly","c":"精確找出;準確指出","s":"Scientists used satellites to pinpoint the source of the oil, and they found a ship that had cleaned its tanks at sea.","t":"科學家利用衛星精確找出油污的來源,並發現了一艘在海上清洗油槽的船。"},{"w":"potent","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or powerful","c":"強效的;有力的","s":"Some sea snails produce a potent poison, so divers should never pick up shells that still have animals inside.","t":"有些海螺會產生強效的毒素,所以潛水員絕不應該撿起裡面還有生物的貝殼。"},{"w":"precarious","p":"adj.","d":"not safe or secure; likely to get worse","c":"不穩定的;岌岌可危的","s":"Many small fishermen are in a precarious situation, because one bad season can leave them without money.","t":"許多小規模漁民處於岌岌可危的處境,因為一個糟糕的漁季就可能讓他們身無分文。"},{"w":"predicament","p":"n.","d":"a difficult situation","c":"困境","s":"The village faced a predicament, because the new port would bring jobs but would also destroy the beach.","t":"村莊面臨一個困境,因為新港口會帶來工作,但也會摧毀海灘。"},{"w":"preclude","p":"v.","d":"to prevent something from happening","c":"排除;阻止","s":"The strong currents preclude swimming at this beach, so visitors can only walk along the sand.","t":"強勁的海流使這片海灘無法游泳,所以遊客只能在沙灘上散步。"},{"w":"prerequisite","p":"n.","d":"something that must exist before something else can happen","c":"先決條件","s":"Clean water is a prerequisite for healthy coral, so the town must stop sewage from entering the bay.","t":"乾淨的水是健康珊瑚的先決條件,所以小鎮必須阻止污水流入海灣。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (pristine – vigorous)","cards":[{"w":"pristine","p":"adj.","d":"completely clean and untouched","c":"原始的;未受污染的","s":"The island's beaches are still pristine, because only a small number of visitors are allowed each day.","t":"這座島的海灘仍然潔淨原始,因為每天只允許少數遊客進入。"},{"w":"prolific","p":"adj.","d":"producing a lot of something","c":"多產的","s":"Cod are prolific breeders that lay millions of eggs, but overfishing still caused their numbers to crash.","t":"鱈魚是多產的繁殖者,一次產下數百萬顆卵,但過度捕撈仍然導致牠們的數量崩跌。"},{"w":"prosper","p":"v.","d":"to be successful, especially by earning money","c":"繁榮;興旺","s":"The village began to prosper after the reef recovered, because divers from around the world came to visit.","t":"珊瑚礁恢復後村莊開始繁榮起來,因為世界各地的潛水客都來造訪。"},{"w":"prudent","p":"adj.","d":"careful and sensible","c":"謹慎的;明智的","s":"It would be prudent to wait before mining the deep sea, because we still know very little about life there.","t":"在開採深海之前先等一等是明智的,因為我們對那裡的生物仍所知甚少。"},{"w":"rampant","p":"adj.","d":"growing or spreading in an uncontrolled way","c":"猖獗的;蔓延的","s":"Illegal fishing is rampant in some areas, so honest fishermen find it hard to earn a fair living.","t":"非法捕魚在某些地區很猖獗,所以誠實的漁民很難賺取合理的生活費。"},{"w":"rectify","p":"v.","d":"to correct something that is wrong","c":"糾正;矯正","s":"The company promised to rectify the damage it caused, and it paid to replant the mangroves along the river.","t":"公司承諾彌補它造成的損害,並出資沿著河岸重新種植紅樹林。"},{"w":"relentless","p":"adj.","d":"continuing strongly without stopping","c":"持續不斷的;無情的","s":"The relentless waves slowly wore away the cliff, so the old house on top is now in danger of falling.","t":"持續不斷的海浪慢慢侵蝕懸崖,所以上面的老房子現在有倒塌的危險。"},{"w":"remedy","p":"n.","d":"a way to solve a problem","c":"補救辦法;解決方法","s":"There is no quick remedy for ocean pollution, but reducing plastic use is an important first step.","t":"海洋污染沒有快速的解決辦法,但減少塑膠使用是重要的第一步。"},{"w":"resurgence","p":"n.","d":"a return of something after a period of decline","c":"復甦;再度興起","s":"There has been a resurgence of humpback whales in the area, and whale-watching tours are now fully booked every summer.","t":"這個地區的座頭鯨數量已經回升,而賞鯨行程現在每年夏天都被訂滿。"},{"w":"revitalise","p":"v.","d":"to give new life and energy to something","c":"使恢復活力;振興","s":"The government plans to revitalise the old fishing port, so it will attract tourists with cafés and a seafood market.","t":"政府計畫振興舊漁港,讓它以咖啡館和海鮮市場吸引遊客。"},{"w":"shortfall","p":"n.","d":"an amount that is less than needed","c":"短缺;不足","s":"There is a shortfall of funding for ocean research, so many important studies have been delayed.","t":"海洋研究的經費不足,所以許多重要的研究被延後了。"},{"w":"skew","p":"v.","d":"to change information so it is not accurate","c":"扭曲;使偏離","s":"A few very large catches can skew the average, so scientists look at many years of data instead.","t":"幾次非常大量的漁獲可能會扭曲平均值,所以科學家改為觀察多年的數據。"},{"w":"steer","p":"v.","d":"to control the direction of a vehicle or situation","c":"操縱;引導","s":"The captain had to steer the boat carefully between the rocks, because the water was very shallow there.","t":"船長必須小心地在岩石之間駕駛船隻,因為那裡的水非常淺。"},{"w":"strive","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to achieve something","c":"努力;奮鬥","s":"The aquarium strives to teach visitors about ocean protection, and every tour ends with tips for reducing plastic.","t":"這間水族館努力教導遊客保護海洋的知識,而每次導覽都以減少塑膠的小訣竅作結。"},{"w":"succumb","p":"v.","d":"to be unable to resist something","c":"屈服;不敵","s":"Many corals succumb to disease after the heatwave, because they were already weak from the hot water.","t":"熱浪過後許多珊瑚不敵疾病而死,因為它們已經被高溫海水削弱了。"},{"w":"surpass","p":"v.","d":"to be better or greater than something","c":"超越;勝過","s":"Plastic in the ocean may surpass the weight of all fish by 2050, unless we change our habits soon.","t":"海洋中的塑膠重量可能在2050年超過所有魚類的重量,除非我們儘快改變習慣。"},{"w":"vast","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large","c":"廣大的;巨大的","s":"The Pacific is so vast that a ship can sail for weeks without seeing land, and few people have crossed it alone.","t":"太平洋如此遼闊,一艘船可以航行好幾週都看不到陸地,而很少人曾獨自橫越它。"},{"w":"vigilant","p":"adj.","d":"watching carefully for danger","c":"警惕的;警覺的","s":"Lifeguards must stay vigilant all day, because a swimmer can get into trouble in just a few seconds.","t":"救生員必須整天保持警覺,因為泳客可能在短短幾秒內就陷入危險。"},{"w":"transient","p":"adj.","d":"staying only for a short time","c":"短暫的;過境的","s":"Many of the whales seen near Taiwan are transient visitors, so they only stay for a few weeks each year.","t":"在台灣附近看到的許多鯨魚是短暫停留的訪客,所以牠們每年只停留幾週。"},{"w":"unravel","p":"v.","d":"to understand or solve something complicated","c":"解開;闡明","s":"Scientists are trying to unravel the mystery of how eels find their way back to the same sea to lay eggs.","t":"科學家正在試著解開鰻魚如何找到路回到同一片海域產卵的謎團。"},{"w":"uphold","p":"v.","d":"to support or defend a law or decision","c":"維護;支持","s":"The court upheld the ban on fishing in the marine park, so the companies that opposed it lost their case.","t":"法院維持了海洋公園內禁止捕魚的禁令,所以反對的公司輸了官司。"},{"w":"versatile","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used in many different ways","c":"多功能的;多才多藝的","s":"Seaweed is a versatile plant, because it can be used in food, medicine and even plastic-free packaging.","t":"海藻是一種用途多樣的植物,因為它可以用在食物、藥品,甚至無塑包裝上。"},{"w":"turbulent","p":"adj.","d":"moving in a strong and uneven way","c":"洶湧的;動盪的","s":"The sea was turbulent after the storm, so the ferry to the island was cancelled for two days.","t":"暴風雨過後海面波濤洶湧,所以前往島上的渡輪停駛了兩天。"},{"w":"wane","p":"v.","d":"to become weaker or smaller","c":"減弱;衰退","s":"Public interest in the oil spill began to wane after a few weeks, but the beach was still polluted.","t":"幾週後大眾對漏油事件的關注開始減弱,但海灘仍然受到污染。"},{"w":"vigorous","p":"adj.","d":"strong, active and full of energy","c":"強健的;有力的","s":"The mangroves showed vigorous growth after they were replanted, and birds soon returned to nest in them.","t":"紅樹林重新種植後展現了旺盛的生長,而鳥類很快就回來在其中築巢。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"marine protected area","p":"n.phr.","d":"a part of the sea where human activities are limited to protect nature","c":"海洋保護區","s":"Fishing is strictly limited inside the marine protected area, so the number of large fish there has doubled in ten years.","t":"海洋保護區內的捕魚受到嚴格限制,所以那裡的大型魚數量在十年內增加了一倍。"},{"w":"sustainable fishing","p":"n.phr.","d":"catching fish in a way that leaves enough to breed","c":"永續漁業","s":"sustainable fishing means leaving enough fish in the sea to breed, so future generations can still enjoy seafood.","t":"永續漁業意味著在海中留下足夠的魚來繁殖,這樣後代子孫仍能享用海鮮。"},{"w":"plastic pollution","p":"n.phr.","d":"harm to nature caused by plastic waste","c":"塑膠污染","s":"plastic pollution is now found even in the deepest trench, so scientists say no part of the ocean is truly untouched.","t":"現在即使在最深的海溝也發現了塑膠污染,所以科學家說海洋沒有任何地方是真正未受影響的。"},{"w":"food web","p":"n.phr.","d":"the network of who eats whom in an ecosystem","c":"食物網","s":"If sharks disappear, the whole food web changes, because the animals they used to eat grow out of control.","t":"如果鯊魚消失,整個食物網都會改變,因為牠們原本捕食的動物會失控地增加。"},{"w":"wash up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be carried onto the shore by the sea","c":"被沖上岸","s":"Every morning, plastic bottles wash up on the beach, and volunteers collect them before the tourists arrive.","t":"每天早上都有塑膠瓶被沖上海灘,志工們會在遊客到達前把它們撿起來。"},{"w":"in deep water","p":"adj.phr.","d":"in serious trouble","c":"陷入困境;麻煩大了","s":"The fishing company is in deep water after it was caught catching sharks illegally, and it may have to close.","t":"這家漁業公司被抓到非法捕撈鯊魚後陷入大麻煩,而且可能必須關門。"},{"w":"out of one's depth","p":"adj.phr.","d":"in a situation that is too difficult for your skills","c":"力不從心;超出能力範圍","s":"I felt completely out of one's depth during the advanced diving course, so I asked the instructor for extra practice.","t":"在進階潛水課程中我覺得完全力不從心,所以我請教練讓我多練習。"},{"w":"make waves","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause trouble or attract attention by doing something new","c":"引起轟動;興風作浪","s":"The young activist began to make waves when her video about ocean plastic went viral, and politicians started to listen.","t":"當這位年輕行動者關於海洋塑膠的影片爆紅時,她開始引起轟動,而政治人物也開始傾聽。"},{"w":"test the waters","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try something carefully to see how people react","c":"試水溫;先試探","s":"The company decided to test the waters by selling paper straws in one city, and then it planned to expand.","t":"這家公司決定先在一個城市販售紙吸管來試水溫,然後計畫再擴大。"},{"w":"rock the boat","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause problems by challenging the way things are","c":"搗亂;破壞現狀","s":"Some fishermen did not want to rock the boat by reporting illegal boats, but one brave captain finally spoke up.","t":"有些漁民不想透過舉報非法船隻來惹麻煩,但一位勇敢的船長終於站了出來。"},{"w":"miss the boat","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose a chance by being too slow","c":"錯失良機","s":"Countries that do not invest in clean ocean energy now may miss the boat, while others lead the new industry.","t":"現在不投資乾淨海洋能源的國家可能會錯失良機,而其他國家則領導這個新產業。"},{"w":"in the same boat","p":"adj.phr.","d":"in the same difficult situation as others","c":"處境相同;同舟共濟","s":"All the fishermen in the village are in the same boat, because the typhoon damaged every boat in the harbour.","t":"村裡所有的漁民都處境相同,因為颱風損壞了港內的每一艘船。"},{"w":"sink or swim","p":"phr.","d":"to succeed or fail without help from others","c":"自生自滅;成敗靠自己","s":"New guides at the diving centre are not left to sink or swim, because experienced divers train them for a month.","t":"潛水中心的新導遊不會被放著自生自滅,因為有經驗的潛水員會訓練他們一個月。"},{"w":"a fish out of water","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who feels uncomfortable in an unfamiliar situation","c":"如魚離水;不自在的人","s":"I felt like a fish out of water at my first diving club meeting, but the other members were very friendly.","t":"我在第一次參加潛水社聚會時覺得渾身不自在,但其他社員都非常友善。"},{"w":"plenty more fish in the sea","p":"phr.","d":"there are many other people or chances available","c":"天涯何處無芳草;機會多的是","s":"My friend was sad after her break-up, so I told her there were plenty more fish in the sea.","t":"我朋友分手後很難過,所以我告訴她天涯何處無芳草。"},{"w":"make a splash","p":"v.phr.","d":"to attract a lot of attention","c":"引起轟動","s":"The student's invention for catching microplastics make a splash at the science fair, and a company offered to help develop it.","t":"那位學生捕捉塑膠微粒的發明在科展上引起轟動,而一家公司提議協助開發它。"},{"w":"all at sea","p":"adj.phr.","d":"confused and not knowing what to do","c":"茫然不知所措","s":"I was all at sea during my first ocean science lecture, but the professor's simple examples helped me understand.","t":"我在第一堂海洋科學課上感到茫然不知所措,但教授簡單的例子幫助我理解了。"},{"w":"high and dry","p":"adj.phr.","d":"left in a difficult situation without help","c":"孤立無援;陷入困境","s":"When the factory closed, hundreds of workers were left high and dry, and many moved away from the fishing town.","t":"工廠關閉時,數百名工人被棄之不顧,而許多人搬離了這個漁港小鎮。"},{"w":"learn the ropes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn how to do a job or activity","c":"學會訣竅;熟悉門道","s":"It took me a whole summer to learn the ropes on my uncle's fishing boat, but now I can help him with almost everything.","t":"我花了一整個夏天才在叔叔的漁船上熟悉門道,但現在幾乎所有事我都能幫他。"},{"w":"a sea change","p":"n.phr.","d":"a complete and important change","c":"徹底的轉變","s":"There has been a sea change in how people see sharks, and many now want to protect them instead of fearing them.","t":"人們看待鯊魚的方式已經有了徹底的轉變,而許多人現在想保護牠們而不是害怕牠們。"}]}];
